  planner_response {
    response: "# Stage 0: Architecture Mapping & Feasibility Report\n\n## 1. Architecture Restatement\n\n**Cloak** is a high-assurance, native Android personal safety application structured into three distinct operational layers designed to maximize user safety and plausible deniability under coercion:\n\n```\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202                      APP ENTRY (Custom Keypad)                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                   \342\224\202 Normal PIN (e.g. 1234)          \342\224\202 Duress PIN (e.g. 9999)\n                   \342\226\274                                 \342\226\274\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220     \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202  LAYER 1: PUBLIC DISGUISE (\"Petal\")  \342\224\202\342\227\204\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244  SILENT SOS CONTROLLER    \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Period Calendar & Cycle Predictor \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Idempotent State Engine\342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Symptom & Mood Tracking           \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Native SMS + Maps URL  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - 15 Evidence-Based Health Tips     \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Periodic GPS Tracking  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - \"Call Gynecologist\" Fake Caller   \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - 5s Audio Chunks Upload \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230     \342\224\202  - 15s Fake-Sleep Screen  \342\224\202\n                   \342\224\202                         \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                   \342\224\202 Hidden 3s Logo Press                  \342\224\202\n                   \342\224\202 (Disabled during SOS)                 \342\224\202\n                   \342\226\274                                       \342\226\274\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220     \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202       LAYER 3: DIGITAL SHIELD        \342\224\202     \342\224\202    SUPABASE BACKEND       \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Photo Sanitizer (Strip EXIF/GPS)  \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - sos_sessions / records \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Digital Lockdown (System Radios)  \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - sos_locations stream   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Burner Notes (Atomic Read & Burn) \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Private Audio Bucket   \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230     \342\224\202  - read_and_burn() RPC    \342\224\202\n                                             \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n1. **Layer 1 \342\200\224 Public Disguise (\342\200\234Petal\342\200\235)**: An authentic, functional menstrual health and cycle tracker. It features calendar visualization, symptom/mood chips, health tips, settings, and a simulated incoming call (\"Call Gynecologist\"). Both Normal and Duress PINs unlock this exact UI with identical visual transitions, ensuring zero disclosure under observation.\n2. **Layer 2 \342\200\224 Guardian & SOS**: The mission-critical safety core. Triggered either by the Duress PIN or a hardware accelerometer pattern (3 spikes $\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart within $1.5\\,\\text{s}$). An idempotent SOS state engine coordinates native SMS dispatches with Google Maps links (`https://maps.google.com/?q=LAT,LNG`), periodic GPS acquisition (~2 min intervals), foreground service microphone chunking (~5s audio blocks) uploaded to Supabase Storage, and a 15-second inactivity \"Fake-Sleep\" blackout screen with a 3-second hold-and-PIN unlock.\n3. **Layer 3 \342\200\224 Digital Shield**: A stealth utility suite accessible only via a covert 3-second logo press (cancelled if movement exceeds 20px, locked during SOS, auto-dismissed on backgrounding). Features a zero-metadata Photo Sanitizer with EXIF verification, a Digital Lockdown control panel shortcut hub, and ephemeral Burner Notes powered by a Supabase atomic `read_and_burn` server function.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Feature Traceability Table\n\n| # | Master Requirement | Architecture Component / Module | Stage | Verification / Test Strategy |\n|---|-------------------|---------------------------------|-------|------------------------------|\n| **1** | First-run setup: Normal & Duress PINs | `feature:auth` / `PinSetupViewModel`, `KeypadView` | Stage 1 | Unit tests for digit validation, non-equality check, and state persistence |\n| **2** | Cryptographic PIN derivation & verification | `core:security` / `CryptoManager` (PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256, 100k iter, random salt) | Stage 1 | JVM tests: constant-time comparison, salt randomness, resistance to timing attack |\n| **3** | Custom 4-digit keypad UI | `feature:auth` / `KeypadScreen` | Stage 1 | Compose UI preview & test: 4-digit masking, backspace, auto-submit |\n| **4** | Identical destination UI for both PINs | `feature:navigation` / `AppNavHost` | Stage 1 | State test: verify NavController routes to Tracker for both inputs |\n| **5** | Duress PIN silently fires SOS | `core:sos` / `SosController` | Stage 1 & 2 | Robolectric test: verify `SosState.Active` emitted without UI alert |\n| **6** | Normal PIN cancels active SOS; Duress maintains it | `core:sos` / `SosController.stopSos()`, `validatePin()` | Stage 1 & 2 | State machine unit tests covering all transition paths |\n| **7** | Shake-to-SOS (3 spikes $\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart, $\\le 1.5\\,\\text{s}$) | `core:sensor` / `ShakeDetector` (Linear acceleration / gravity-filtered) | Stage 2 | Synthetic sensor event replay test & physical device shake test |\n| **8** | Support Circle: up to 3 emergency contacts | `feature:contacts` / `ContactRepository`, Room DB | Stage 2 | Room DAO unit tests; UI tests for adding/editing 1\342\200\2233 phone numbers |\n| **9** | Native SMS dispatch via `SmsManager` | `core:telephony` / `SmsDispatcher` | Stage 2 | Unit test for SMS payload formatting; real SIM physical device test |\n| **10** | Google Maps link with coordinates (`https://maps.google.com/?q=...`) | `core:location` / `LocationFormatter` | Stage 2 | Regex unit test validating format and query coordinate bounds |\n| **11** | Location fallback: Last known first, then fresh fix | `core:location` / `LocationProvider` (`FusedLocationProviderClient`) | Stage 2 | Mock location provider tests + real GPS device verification |\n| **12** | Periodic location updates (~2 minutes during SOS) | `core:sos` / `SosLocationPoller` | Stage 2 | Coroutine test scheduler validating 120s dispatch cadence |\n| **13** | Audio recording in ~5-second chunks | `core:audio` / `AudioChunkRecorder` (`MediaRecorder` / `AudioRecord`) | Stage 3 | Local file test: verify chunk duration, AAC encoding, file creation |\n| **14** | Foreground Service for recording & notifications | `service` / `SosForegroundService` (type: `microphone`, `location`) | Stage 3 | Android Service lifecycle test with ongoing notification verification |\n| **15** | Supabase Storage audio upload with retry logic | `data:network` / `SupabaseStorageRepository` | Stage 3 | MockWebServer test: 3-tier exponential backoff and offline queueing |\n| **16** | SOS metadata & location persistence in Supabase | `data:network` / `SupabaseSosRepository` | Stage 3 | Supabase REST client tests verifying RLS-compliant payloads |\n| **17** | Fake-Sleep blackout screen (15s inactivity) | `feature:fakesleep` / `FakeSleepOverlay` | Stage 3 | Compose state timer test; black screen rendering check |\n| **18** | Fake-Sleep exit: 3-second hold + PIN keypad | `feature:fakesleep` / `FakeSleepUnlockGesture` | Stage 3 | Pointer input gesture test (3000ms continuous press) |\n| **19** | Optional WhatsApp relay (`wa.me` intent) | `core:telephony` / `WhatsAppRelay` | Stage 3 | Intent verification unit test |\n| **20** | Period & Health Tracker disguise: Calendar, log, tips | `feature:tracker` / `CalendarScreen`, `LogScreen`, `TipsScreen` | Stage 4 | UI tests: cycle date math, 15 tip cards display, symptom chip toggling |\n| **21** | \"Call Gynecologist\" simulated incoming call | `feature:tracker` / `FakeCallScreen` (Normal=Mom, Long=Police) | Stage 4 | UI interaction tests: ringtone playback, caller name toggles |\n| **22** | Secret Shield gesture: 3s hold, 20px delta cancel | `feature:shield` / `SecretGestureDetector` | Stage 5 | Compose PointerInput test: cancellation on $\\Delta > 20\\text{px}$, haptic event |\n| **23** | Shield SOS lockout & background auto-dismiss | `feature:shield` / `ShieldViewModel` | Stage 5 | Lifecycle test: `ON_STOP` triggers backstack pop to root |\n| **24** | Photo Sanitizer: EXIF strip, re-encode, verify | `feature:shield` / `PhotoSanitizer` (`ExifInterface`, JPEG decode/compress) | Stage 5 | Unit tests: inspect input image with GPS vs output image with zero EXIF tags |\n| **25** | Digital Lockdown: System Settings panel intents | `feature:shield` / `DigitalLockdownLauncher` | Stage 5 | Intent verification: `ACTION_WIFI_SETTINGS`, `ACTION_BLUETOOTH_SETTINGS`, `ACTION_LOCATION_SOURCE_SETTINGS` |\n| **26** | Burner Notes: 6-digit code, atomic read-and-burn | `feature:shield` / `BurnerNoteRepository`, Supabase RPC | Stage 5 | Integration test: verify first fetch returns note, second fetch returns 404/destroyed |\n| **27** | End-to-end integration & release build | Whole app | Stage 6 | Full test suite execution, Gradle release build, 90-second demo script |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Android Platform Feasibility, Permissions, & Lifecycle Constraints\n\n### A. Background Microphone & Audio Chunking (Android 14+ / API 34+)\n- **OS Constraint**: Android 14 introduces strict foreground service types. Starting audio recording when the app is in the background is blocked by the OS (`SecurityException: Foreground service type microphone not allowed to start from background`).\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  1. `SosForegroundService` is declared in `AndroidManifest.xml` with `android:foregroundServiceType=\"microphone|location|shortService\"`.\n  2. The service is launched **while the app is in the foreground** (at the exact moment Duress PIN is verified or Shake is detected).\n  3. A persistent, discreet system notification is posted as mandated by Android.\n  4. Audio chunks are written to application cache (`context.cacheDir/sos_audio/`) using `MediaRecorder` configured for `MPEG_4` / `AAC`, cycled cleanly every 5,000 ms, and dispatched to a background coroutine upload worker.\n  5. **Lifecycle Disclosure**: If the Android system terminates the process due to extreme memory pressure, recording stops. The app will never make misleading claims that recording survives a process kill.\n\n### B. Fake-Sleep vs. Native Lock Screen\n- **OS Constraint**: An app cannot genuinely turn off the device screen or replace the native Android OS lock screen without Device Admin/Owner privileges (which would flag the app and defeat plausible deniability).\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - Fake-Sleep is implemented in-app as an opaque, pure-black (`#000000`) full-screen surface that overrides system brightness to minimum while holding a wake lock (`FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON`).\n  - This keeps the app in the **resumed foreground lifecycle state**, enabling uninterrupted microphone recording, accelerometer monitoring, and GPS polling without falling into OS-level Doze mode.\n\n### C. Native SMS Sending (`SmsManager`) & Google Play Policies\n- **OS Constraint**: Direct SMS dispatch via `SmsManager.sendTextMessage()` requires `SEND_SMS`. Google Play restricts `SEND_SMS` exclusively to default SMS handlers or specific vetted safety exceptions.\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - The app implements native `SmsManager` dispatch as the primary safety mechanism for sideloaded/direct-install use.\n  - A fallback intent flow (`Intent.ACTION_SENDTO` to `smsto:`) is provided as an alternative if `SEND_SMS` is denied or when targeting standard Play Store distribution.\n  - Clear user disclosure states that delivery depends on cellular carrier coverage, SIM availability, and signal strength.\n\n### D. Hardware Radios (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, GPS)\n- **OS Constraint**: Since Android 10 (Q), third-party applications are forbidden from silently toggling Wi-Fi (`WifiManager.setWifiEnabled()` returns false/deprecated) and Bluetooth (`BluetoothAdapter.disable()` restricted).\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - \"Digital Lockdown\" provides instant, frictionless deep-link shortcuts to system settings panels:\n    - Wi-Fi: `Settings.Panel.ACTION_WIFI` (or `Settings.ACTION_WIFI_SETTINGS`)\n    - Bluetooth: `Settings.ACTION_BLUETOOTH_SETTINGS`\n    - Location: `Settings.ACTION_LOCATION_SOURCE_SETTINGS`\n  - Explicit UI copy states: \"Opens system control panel to disable device radio antennas.\"\n\n### E. WhatsApp Relay\n- **OS Constraint**: WhatsApp does not expose an API for third-party apps to send messages in the background without user confirmation.\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - Uses standard URI intent: `https://api.whatsapp.com/send?phone=+1234567890&text=...`.\n  - Disclosed as a manual one-tap user relay, never claiming automated background delivery.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Proposed Native Kotlin Project Structure\n\n```\napp/src/main/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AndroidManifest.xml\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 java/com/example/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 MainActivity.kt                      # Single activity, window insets, edge-to-edge\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CloakApplication.kt                  # Application class, DI/container initialization\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 core/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 audio/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AudioChunkRecorder.kt        # 5-second chunk recorder with MediaRecorder\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AudioFileManager.kt          # Temp file cleanup and retention\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 location/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LocationProvider.kt          # FusedLocationProviderClient wrapper\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 LocationFormatter.kt         # Maps URL builder & formatting\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 security/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CryptoManager.kt             # PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256, secure salt generation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 PinStorage.kt                # EncryptedSharedPreferences for PIN hashes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 sensor/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ShakeDetector.kt             # SensorEventListener for gravity-free spikes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 telephony/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SmsDispatcher.kt             # SmsManager native sender + intent fallback\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 WhatsAppRelay.kt             # wa.me intent launcher\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 local/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CloakDatabase.kt             # Room DB for contacts & period logs\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ContactDao.kt                # Support circle DAO\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PeriodDao.kt                 # Cycle logs DAO\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 entity/                      # EmergencyContact, PeriodEntry entities\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 network/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseConfig.kt            # Supabase URL & public anon key config\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseClient.kt            # OkHttp / Retrofit HTTP client for Supabase REST\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseSosRepository.kt     # sos_sessions & sos_locations API calls\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseStorageRepository.kt # Storage bucket audio uploads with retry\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 BurnerNoteRepository.kt      # read_and_burn RPC integration\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 repository/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ContactRepository.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 PeriodRepository.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 service/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SosForegroundService.kt          # Audio & location foreground service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ui/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 navigation/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Screen.kt                    # Type-safe navigation routes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AppNavHost.kt                # Root Navigation host with BackHandler\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Color.kt                     # M3 Color palette (Blush, Rose, Slate)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Theme.kt                     # Petal Material3 Theme\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Type.kt                      # Clean typography\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 KeypadScreen.kt              # Discreet 4-digit PIN pad\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PinSetupScreen.kt            # First-run Normal & Duress setup\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthViewModel.kt             # PIN verification & routing logic\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tracker/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 TrackerMainScreen.kt         # Scaffold with Bottom Navigation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CalendarTab.kt               # Menstrual cycle calendar & predictions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LogTab.kt                    # Symptom & mood chip logging\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 TipsTab.kt                   # 15 evidence-based wellness cards\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SettingsTab.kt               # Support circle contacts & preferences\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 FakeCallScreen.kt            # \"Call Gynecologist\" incoming call UI\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 TrackerViewModel.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 shield/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ShieldDashboardScreen.kt     # Secret 3-tile dashboard\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PhotoSanitizerScreen.kt      # EXIF strip, photo picker, save clean copy\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DigitalLockdownScreen.kt     # Radio toggle deep-links\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 BurnerNotesScreen.kt         # Ephemeral note writer & code retriever\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ShieldViewModel.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 fakesleep/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 FakeSleepOverlay.kt          # Black screen with 3s hold-to-unlock\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 util/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ExifStripper.kt                  # ExifInterface cleaner & JPEG re-encoder\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 GestureExtensions.kt             # 3-second hold with pixel threshold detector\n```\n\n### Gradle & Dependency Plan (`app/build.gradle.kts`)\n- **AndroidX & Jetpack Compose**: Compose BOM, Material3, Navigation Compose, Lifecycle Runtime Compose.\n- **Room Persistence**: `androidx.room:room-runtime`, `androidx.room:room-ktx`, `androidx.room:room-compiler` (KSP).\n- **Networking & JSON**: `com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp`, `com.squareup.retrofit2:retrofit`, `com.squareup.moshi:moshi-kotlin`.\n- **Hardware & Sensors**: Native `android.hardware.SensorManager`, `com.google.android.gms:play-services-location`.\n- **Media & EXIF**: `androidx.exifinterface:exifinterface`.\n- **Testing**: JUnit4, Robolectric 4.14+, Compose UI Test, Kotlin Coroutines Test.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Required Android Permissions & Justifications\n\n| Permission | Protection Level | Functional Justification |\n|------------|------------------|--------------------------|\n| `android.permission.INTERNET` | Normal | Uploading SOS audio chunks, persisting SOS locations, and communicating with Supabase REST API / Burner Notes. |\n| `android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE` | Normal | Detecting active internet connectivity to trigger offline queue retries. |\n| `android.permission.VIBRATE` | Normal | Providing subtle haptic feedback for the 3-second hidden Shield gesture and keypad interactions. |\n| `android.permission.SEND_SMS` | Dangerous | Sending urgent SOS alerts with GPS coordinates to Support Circle contacts during duress or shake trigger. |\n| `android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION` | Dangerous | Acquiring high-accuracy GPS coordinates for emergency SMS and live tracking updates. |\n| `android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION` | Dangerous | Fallback approximate cell/Wi-Fi location when GPS lock is slow or indoors. |\n| `android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO` | Dangerous | Capturing 5-second audio evidence chunks during an active SOS emergency session. |\n| `android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE` | Normal | Running the uninterrupted SOS safety session when the screen is dimmed or Fake-Sleep is active. |\n| `android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MICROPHONE` | Normal | Mandated by Android 14+ for recording audio from a background service. |\n| `android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION` | Normal | Mandated by Android 14+ for streaming location fixes during an active SOS service. |\n| `android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS` | Dangerous (API 33+) | Displaying the system-required persistent notification for foreground service operation. |\n| `android.permission.WAKE_LOCK` | Normal | Keeping the CPU active to prevent the device from entering deep sleep during Fake-Sleep audio upload. |\n\n*Note: For the Photo Sanitizer, modern zero-permission Android Photo Picker (`ActivityResultContracts.PickVisualMedia`) and `MediaStore` Scoped Storage will be used, eliminating the need for broad storage permissions (`READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`).*\n\n---\n\n## 6. Supabase Backend Architecture & Schema Plan\n\n### A. SQL Schema & Row Level Security (RLS)\n\n```sql\n-- 1. SOS SESSIONS TABLE\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.sos_sessions (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    session_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    trigger_source TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (trigger_source IN (\'duress_pin\', \'shake\', \'manual_test\')),\n    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \'active\' CHECK (status IN (\'active\', \'resolved\', \'cancelled\')),\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT timezone(\'utc\', now()),\n    ended_at TIMESTAMPTZ\n);\n\nALTER TABLE public.sos_sessions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- Allow anonymous client to insert sessions (write-only)\nCREATE POLICY \"Allow anon insert to sos_sessions\" \nON public.sos_sessions FOR INSERT \nTO anon WITH CHECK (true);\n\n-- Deny public reading of all SOS sessions\nCREATE POLICY \"Deny anon select to sos_sessions\" \nON public.sos_sessions FOR SELECT \nTO anon USING (false);\n\n-- 2. SOS LOCATIONS TABLE\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.sos_locations (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    session_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES public.sos_sessions(session_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    latitude DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,\n    longitude DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,\n    accuracy REAL,\n    recorded_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT timezone(\'utc\', now())\n);\n\nALTER TABLE public.sos_locations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Allow anon insert to sos_locations\" \nON public.sos_locations FOR INSERT \nTO anon WITH CHECK (true);\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Deny anon select to sos_locations\" \nON public.sos_locations FOR SELECT \nTO anon USING (false);\n\n-- 3. BURNER NOTES TABLE\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.burner_notes (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    access_code TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    note_body TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT timezone(\'utc\', now()),\n    expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT (timezone(\'utc\', now()) + INTERVAL \'24 hours\')\n);\n\nALTER TABLE public.burner_notes ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- Clients can insert a note with code\nCREATE POLICY \"Allow anon insert to burner_notes\" \nON public.burner_notes FOR INSERT \nTO anon WITH CHECK (char_length(access_code) = 6);\n\n-- Clients cannot directly query or list burner_notes table\nCREATE POLICY \"Deny direct anon select to burner_notes\" \nON public.burner_notes FOR SELECT \nTO anon USING (false);\n\n-- 4. ATOMIC READ-AND-BURN DATABASE FUNCTION\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.read_and_burn(p_code TEXT)\nRETURNS TABLE (note_content TEXT, is_valid BOOLEAN)\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n    v_note_body TEXT;\nBEGIN\n    -- Delete and return in a single atomic transaction\n    DELETE FROM public.burner_notes\n    WHERE access_code = p_code\n      AND expires_at > timezone(\'utc\', now())\n    RETURNING note_body INTO v_note_body;\n\n    IF v_note_body IS NOT NULL THEN\n        RETURN QUERY SELECT v_note_body AS note_content, true AS is_valid;\n    ELSE\n        RETURN QUERY SELECT NULL::TEXT AS note_content, false AS is_valid;\n    END IF;\nEND;\n$$;\n\n-- 5. STORAGE BUCKET CONFIGURATION\n-- Bucket: \'sos_audio\' (Private)\n-- Policy: Anon role can upload files into their own session prefix: session_id/*\n-- Policy: Anon cannot list or download files from the bucket\n```\n\n### B. Client Security Policy\n- The Android client will only use the public **Anon Key** and **Project URL**, injected via `.env` / `BuildConfig`.\n- Under no circumstances will a service-role key or master database credential be included in the APK.\n- All writes are blind inserts into RLS-protected tables; reads are strictly prohibited except via the atomic `read_and_burn` RPC function.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Windows Setup, Build, & PowerShell Test Commands\n\nThe user\'s project location is `D:\\CloakNative`. Below are the exact Windows PowerShell commands:\n\n### A. Environment Verification\n```powershell\n# Verify Java 17+ and Git\njava -version\ngit --version\n```\n\n### B. Project Setup & Validation (in `D:\\CloakNative`)\n```powershell\nSet-Location -Path \"D:\\CloakNative\"\n\n# Check Gradle status and clean state\ngradle --version\n```\n\n### C. Build & Compile Test\n```powershell\n# Compile the native debug APK\ngradle :app:assembleDebug\n```\n\n### D. Unit & Robolectric Test Execution\n```powershell\n# Run all unit and JVM-based Robolectric tests with detailed test report\ngradle :app:testDebugUnitTest --info\n```\n\n### E. Install on Connected Real Device / Emulator\n```powershell\n# Install debug build on connected Android device via ADB\nadb devices\ngradle :app:installDebug\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Feasibility & Implementation Classification\n\n### A. Fully Implementable in Native Android & Automated Testable\n1. Cryptographic PIN derivation (PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256), salt generator, and constant-time verifier.\n2. Custom 4-digit keypad UI, auto-submit, backspace, and masking.\n3. Centralized idempotent SOS state engine with event emission (`SosState.Idle`, `SosState.Active`, `SosState.Stopped`).\n4. Fake-Sleep UI overlay, 15s countdown timer, and 3-second hold gesture detector.\n5. Menstrual cycle calculations, 28-day prediction algorithm, symptom chip states, and 15 wellness cards.\n6. \"Call Gynecologist\" incoming call UI simulation with custom caller name.\n7. Hidden 3-second logo press with 20px movement cancellation and background auto-dismissal.\n8. Photo Sanitizer EXIF stripper removing all GPS/device tags and verifying output stream.\n9. Room database persistence for emergency contacts and local cycle logs.\n10. Supabase REST payloads and atomic `read_and_burn` RPC consumer.\n\n### B. Requires Real Device Testing\n1. **Physical Accelerometer Shake Detection**: Validating the 3-spike $\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ threshold under real-world movement (walking, sitting, pocket movement vs. intentional vigorous shake).\n2. **Native SMS Dispatch**: Verification with real cellular SIM carrier, handling airplane mode, unprovisioned SIM, and signal loss.\n3. **Hardware GPS Fix**: Verifying transition from last known location to high-precision satellite fix indoors vs. outdoors.\n4. **Haptic Vibration**: Physical tactile feel of the short vibration confirming secret Shield entry.\n\n### C. Android Platform Constraints & Safe Behaviors\n1. **Background Microphone Recording**: Must use a Foreground Service started while the app is active; Android OS displays a privacy indicator dot.\n2. **Silent Radio Toggling**: Android restricts third-party apps from silently toggling Wi-Fi/Bluetooth; the app provides one-tap system setting panel shortcuts.\n3. **Automated WhatsApp Dispatch**: WhatsApp has no silent send API; implemented as a direct pre-filled `wa.me` intent.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Stage Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n### Stage 1: Project Foundation & Secure PIN\n- [ ] Native Kotlin Jetpack Compose project compiles cleanly with zero warnings/errors.\n- [ ] First-run wizard prompts user to set Normal PIN and Duress PIN (rejects identical PINs).\n- [ ] Salted PBKDF2 hash stored securely; constant-time comparison prevents timing attacks.\n- [ ] Custom 4-digit keypad unlocks into the disguise tracker for both PINs.\n- [ ] Entering Duress PIN triggers `SosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")` in background.\n- [ ] Normal PIN verifies without triggering SOS.\n\n### Stage 2: Core SOS, Contacts, Location, & SMS\n- [ ] Support Circle screen allows adding, viewing, and deleting up to 3 emergency contacts in Room DB.\n- [ ] `ShakeDetector` reliably identifies 3 acceleration spikes ($\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart within $1.5\\,\\text{s}$).\n- [ ] Central SOS state machine is idempotent: duplicate triggers do not cause multiple simultaneous dispatches.\n- [ ] Native SMS sent via `SmsManager` with Google Maps link: `https://maps.google.com/?q=LAT,LNG`.\n- [ ] Fallback to last known location first, transitioning to fresh location updates every ~2 minutes.\n- [ ] Entering Normal PIN stops active SOS; Duress PIN keeps SOS active while returning to tracker.\n\n### Stage 3: Audio Chunks, Supabase Upload, & Fake-Sleep\n- [ ] `SosForegroundService` captures audio in ~5-second AAC chunks with ongoing notification.\n- [ ] Audio chunks uploaded to Supabase Storage bucket with exponential backoff on network failure.\n- [ ] SOS session status and location stream logged in `sos_sessions` and `sos_locations`.\n- [ ] After 15 seconds of inactivity during active SOS, screen goes completely black (Fake-Sleep).\n- [ ] 3-second continuous hold on Fake-Sleep reveals PIN keypad.\n- [ ] Normal PIN exits Fake-Sleep and stops SOS; Duress PIN returns to tracker while maintaining SOS.\n\n### Stage 4: Public Disguise Tracker & Simulated Call\n- [ ] Calendar displays marked period days, predicted next cycle days, and symptom dots.\n- [ ] Symptom chips and mood selection persist to local database.\n- [ ] Scrolling Tips screen renders 15 evidence-based women\'s health cards.\n- [ ] \"Call Gynecologist\" card launches realistic incoming phone call screen.\n- [ ] Normal tap displays \"Mom\"; long press displays \"Police\"; ringtone plays with graceful fallback.\n\n### Stage 5: Digital Shield\n- [ ] 3-second hold on top-left logo with $< 20\\,\\text{px}$ movement triggers haptic pulse and opens Shield.\n- [ ] Shield gesture is locked out while SOS is active.\n- [ ] Shield automatically dismisses to root tracker when app is backgrounded (`ON_STOP`).\n- [ ] Photo Sanitizer strips all EXIF tags (GPS, camera model, date) and verifies clean output.\n- [ ] Digital Lockdown shortcuts open system panels for Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and Location.\n- [ ] Burner Notes creates note with 6-digit code; atomic RPC deletes note upon first retrieval; second attempt confirms destruction.\n\n### Stage 6: Hardening, Release Build, & 90-Second Demo\n- [ ] All unit and Robolectric tests pass (`gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`).\n- [ ] Release APK built without warnings (`gradle :app:assembleRelease`).\n- [ ] End-to-end verification report documenting verified vs. platform-constrained features.\n- [ ] 90-second clear demo script prepared.\n\n---\n\n**Stage 0 is complete. Awaiting your approval before proceeding to Stage 1.**"
    thinking: "**Analyzing Stage 0 Details**\n\nI have successfully completed the build! I\'m now meticulously examining the prompt for Stage 0\'s specific requirements. I\'m focusing on extracting the precise components needed for the initial response: the feature traceability table, project structure, feasibility, Supabase plan, acceptance criteria, and Windows strategy. The goal is to ensure absolute alignment with the instructions.\n\n\n**Clarifying Project Boundaries**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on the constraints, specifically ensuring that no implementation code is generated until explicitly approved. I\'m carefully delineating the scope for Stage 0, zeroing in on architecture mapping and feasibility. I\'m preparing to restate the architecture and develop the feature traceability table, meticulously mapping every requirement. My immediate priorities are limitations and permissions, followed by the native Kotlin project\'s structure and Supabase configuration. I\'ll define Windows PowerShell commands and formulate a comprehensive checklist to capture all critical aspects, while ensuring implementation isn\'t accidentally started.\n\n\n**Defining Stage 0 Deliverables**\n\nI\'m solidifying the acceptance criteria for each stage, clarifying what constitutes a successful Stage 0. The central focus now is creating all nine detailed deliverables, adhering to a professional and technical standard. I\'m carefully reviewing all prompt requirements, including both the internal and public names, and the features for Layers 1 and 2. My attention is particularly on the precise requirements for each feature, especially in Layer 2.\n\n\n**Outlining Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now diving into the detailed feature breakdown for Layer 3, particularly the \"Digital Shield.\" I\'m parsing the requirements for the secret gesture activation, including haptic feedback and the auto-close function. I\'m also mapping the photo sanitizer and digital lockdown features, including integration with the system settings. The burner notes with the random code and atomic read/burn function are also in view.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# Stage 0: Architecture Mapping & Feasibility Report\n\n## 1. Architecture Restatement\n\n**Cloak** is a high-assurance, native Android personal safety application structured into three distinct operational layers designed to maximize user safety and plausible deniability under coercion:\n\n```\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202                      APP ENTRY (Custom Keypad)                         \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                   \342\224\202 Normal PIN (e.g. 1234)          \342\224\202 Duress PIN (e.g. 9999)\n                   \342\226\274                                 \342\226\274\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220     \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202  LAYER 1: PUBLIC DISGUISE (\"Petal\")  \342\224\202\342\227\204\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244  SILENT SOS CONTROLLER    \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Period Calendar & Cycle Predictor \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Idempotent State Engine\342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Symptom & Mood Tracking           \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Native SMS + Maps URL  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - 15 Evidence-Based Health Tips     \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Periodic GPS Tracking  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - \"Call Gynecologist\" Fake Caller   \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - 5s Audio Chunks Upload \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230     \342\224\202  - 15s Fake-Sleep Screen  \342\224\202\n                   \342\224\202                         \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                   \342\224\202 Hidden 3s Logo Press                  \342\224\202\n                   \342\224\202 (Disabled during SOS)                 \342\224\202\n                   \342\226\274                                       \342\226\274\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220     \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202       LAYER 3: DIGITAL SHIELD        \342\224\202     \342\224\202    SUPABASE BACKEND       \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Photo Sanitizer (Strip EXIF/GPS)  \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - sos_sessions / records \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Digital Lockdown (System Radios)  \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - sos_locations stream   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  - Burner Notes (Atomic Read & Burn) \342\224\202     \342\224\202  - Private Audio Bucket   \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230     \342\224\202  - read_and_burn() RPC    \342\224\202\n                                             \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n1. **Layer 1 \342\200\224 Public Disguise (\342\200\234Petal\342\200\235)**: An authentic, functional menstrual health and cycle tracker. It features calendar visualization, symptom/mood chips, health tips, settings, and a simulated incoming call (\"Call Gynecologist\"). Both Normal and Duress PINs unlock this exact UI with identical visual transitions, ensuring zero disclosure under observation.\n2. **Layer 2 \342\200\224 Guardian & SOS**: The mission-critical safety core. Triggered either by the Duress PIN or a hardware accelerometer pattern (3 spikes $\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart within $1.5\\,\\text{s}$). An idempotent SOS state engine coordinates native SMS dispatches with Google Maps links (`https://maps.google.com/?q=LAT,LNG`), periodic GPS acquisition (~2 min intervals), foreground service microphone chunking (~5s audio blocks) uploaded to Supabase Storage, and a 15-second inactivity \"Fake-Sleep\" blackout screen with a 3-second hold-and-PIN unlock.\n3. **Layer 3 \342\200\224 Digital Shield**: A stealth utility suite accessible only via a covert 3-second logo press (cancelled if movement exceeds 20px, locked during SOS, auto-dismissed on backgrounding). Features a zero-metadata Photo Sanitizer with EXIF verification, a Digital Lockdown control panel shortcut hub, and ephemeral Burner Notes powered by a Supabase atomic `read_and_burn` server function.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Feature Traceability Table\n\n| # | Master Requirement | Architecture Component / Module | Stage | Verification / Test Strategy |\n|---|-------------------|---------------------------------|-------|------------------------------|\n| **1** | First-run setup: Normal & Duress PINs | `feature:auth` / `PinSetupViewModel`, `KeypadView` | Stage 1 | Unit tests for digit validation, non-equality check, and state persistence |\n| **2** | Cryptographic PIN derivation & verification | `core:security` / `CryptoManager` (PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256, 100k iter, random salt) | Stage 1 | JVM tests: constant-time comparison, salt randomness, resistance to timing attack |\n| **3** | Custom 4-digit keypad UI | `feature:auth` / `KeypadScreen` | Stage 1 | Compose UI preview & test: 4-digit masking, backspace, auto-submit |\n| **4** | Identical destination UI for both PINs | `feature:navigation` / `AppNavHost` | Stage 1 | State test: verify NavController routes to Tracker for both inputs |\n| **5** | Duress PIN silently fires SOS | `core:sos` / `SosController` | Stage 1 & 2 | Robolectric test: verify `SosState.Active` emitted without UI alert |\n| **6** | Normal PIN cancels active SOS; Duress maintains it | `core:sos` / `SosController.stopSos()`, `validatePin()` | Stage 1 & 2 | State machine unit tests covering all transition paths |\n| **7** | Shake-to-SOS (3 spikes $\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart, $\\le 1.5\\,\\text{s}$) | `core:sensor` / `ShakeDetector` (Linear acceleration / gravity-filtered) | Stage 2 | Synthetic sensor event replay test & physical device shake test |\n| **8** | Support Circle: up to 3 emergency contacts | `feature:contacts` / `ContactRepository`, Room DB | Stage 2 | Room DAO unit tests; UI tests for adding/editing 1\342\200\2233 phone numbers |\n| **9** | Native SMS dispatch via `SmsManager` | `core:telephony` / `SmsDispatcher` | Stage 2 | Unit test for SMS payload formatting; real SIM physical device test |\n| **10** | Google Maps link with coordinates (`https://maps.google.com/?q=...`) | `core:location` / `LocationFormatter` | Stage 2 | Regex unit test validating format and query coordinate bounds |\n| **11** | Location fallback: Last known first, then fresh fix | `core:location` / `LocationProvider` (`FusedLocationProviderClient`) | Stage 2 | Mock location provider tests + real GPS device verification |\n| **12** | Periodic location updates (~2 minutes during SOS) | `core:sos` / `SosLocationPoller` | Stage 2 | Coroutine test scheduler validating 120s dispatch cadence |\n| **13** | Audio recording in ~5-second chunks | `core:audio` / `AudioChunkRecorder` (`MediaRecorder` / `AudioRecord`) | Stage 3 | Local file test: verify chunk duration, AAC encoding, file creation |\n| **14** | Foreground Service for recording & notifications | `service` / `SosForegroundService` (type: `microphone`, `location`) | Stage 3 | Android Service lifecycle test with ongoing notification verification |\n| **15** | Supabase Storage audio upload with retry logic | `data:network` / `SupabaseStorageRepository` | Stage 3 | MockWebServer test: 3-tier exponential backoff and offline queueing |\n| **16** | SOS metadata & location persistence in Supabase | `data:network` / `SupabaseSosRepository` | Stage 3 | Supabase REST client tests verifying RLS-compliant payloads |\n| **17** | Fake-Sleep blackout screen (15s inactivity) | `feature:fakesleep` / `FakeSleepOverlay` | Stage 3 | Compose state timer test; black screen rendering check |\n| **18** | Fake-Sleep exit: 3-second hold + PIN keypad | `feature:fakesleep` / `FakeSleepUnlockGesture` | Stage 3 | Pointer input gesture test (3000ms continuous press) |\n| **19** | Optional WhatsApp relay (`wa.me` intent) | `core:telephony` / `WhatsAppRelay` | Stage 3 | Intent verification unit test |\n| **20** | Period & Health Tracker disguise: Calendar, log, tips | `feature:tracker` / `CalendarScreen`, `LogScreen`, `TipsScreen` | Stage 4 | UI tests: cycle date math, 15 tip cards display, symptom chip toggling |\n| **21** | \"Call Gynecologist\" simulated incoming call | `feature:tracker` / `FakeCallScreen` (Normal=Mom, Long=Police) | Stage 4 | UI interaction tests: ringtone playback, caller name toggles |\n| **22** | Secret Shield gesture: 3s hold, 20px delta cancel | `feature:shield` / `SecretGestureDetector` | Stage 5 | Compose PointerInput test: cancellation on $\\Delta > 20\\text{px}$, haptic event |\n| **23** | Shield SOS lockout & background auto-dismiss | `feature:shield` / `ShieldViewModel` | Stage 5 | Lifecycle test: `ON_STOP` triggers backstack pop to root |\n| **24** | Photo Sanitizer: EXIF strip, re-encode, verify | `feature:shield` / `PhotoSanitizer` (`ExifInterface`, JPEG decode/compress) | Stage 5 | Unit tests: inspect input image with GPS vs output image with zero EXIF tags |\n| **25** | Digital Lockdown: System Settings panel intents | `feature:shield` / `DigitalLockdownLauncher` | Stage 5 | Intent verification: `ACTION_WIFI_SETTINGS`, `ACTION_BLUETOOTH_SETTINGS`, `ACTION_LOCATION_SOURCE_SETTINGS` |\n| **26** | Burner Notes: 6-digit code, atomic read-and-burn | `feature:shield` / `BurnerNoteRepository`, Supabase RPC | Stage 5 | Integration test: verify first fetch returns note, second fetch returns 404/destroyed |\n| **27** | End-to-end integration & release build | Whole app | Stage 6 | Full test suite execution, Gradle release build, 90-second demo script |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Android Platform Feasibility, Permissions, & Lifecycle Constraints\n\n### A. Background Microphone & Audio Chunking (Android 14+ / API 34+)\n- **OS Constraint**: Android 14 introduces strict foreground service types. Starting audio recording when the app is in the background is blocked by the OS (`SecurityException: Foreground service type microphone not allowed to start from background`).\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  1. `SosForegroundService` is declared in `AndroidManifest.xml` with `android:foregroundServiceType=\"microphone|location|shortService\"`.\n  2. The service is launched **while the app is in the foreground** (at the exact moment Duress PIN is verified or Shake is detected).\n  3. A persistent, discreet system notification is posted as mandated by Android.\n  4. Audio chunks are written to application cache (`context.cacheDir/sos_audio/`) using `MediaRecorder` configured for `MPEG_4` / `AAC`, cycled cleanly every 5,000 ms, and dispatched to a background coroutine upload worker.\n  5. **Lifecycle Disclosure**: If the Android system terminates the process due to extreme memory pressure, recording stops. The app will never make misleading claims that recording survives a process kill.\n\n### B. Fake-Sleep vs. Native Lock Screen\n- **OS Constraint**: An app cannot genuinely turn off the device screen or replace the native Android OS lock screen without Device Admin/Owner privileges (which would flag the app and defeat plausible deniability).\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - Fake-Sleep is implemented in-app as an opaque, pure-black (`#000000`) full-screen surface that overrides system brightness to minimum while holding a wake lock (`FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON`).\n  - This keeps the app in the **resumed foreground lifecycle state**, enabling uninterrupted microphone recording, accelerometer monitoring, and GPS polling without falling into OS-level Doze mode.\n\n### C. Native SMS Sending (`SmsManager`) & Google Play Policies\n- **OS Constraint**: Direct SMS dispatch via `SmsManager.sendTextMessage()` requires `SEND_SMS`. Google Play restricts `SEND_SMS` exclusively to default SMS handlers or specific vetted safety exceptions.\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - The app implements native `SmsManager` dispatch as the primary safety mechanism for sideloaded/direct-install use.\n  - A fallback intent flow (`Intent.ACTION_SENDTO` to `smsto:`) is provided as an alternative if `SEND_SMS` is denied or when targeting standard Play Store distribution.\n  - Clear user disclosure states that delivery depends on cellular carrier coverage, SIM availability, and signal strength.\n\n### D. Hardware Radios (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, GPS)\n- **OS Constraint**: Since Android 10 (Q), third-party applications are forbidden from silently toggling Wi-Fi (`WifiManager.setWifiEnabled()` returns false/deprecated) and Bluetooth (`BluetoothAdapter.disable()` restricted).\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - \"Digital Lockdown\" provides instant, frictionless deep-link shortcuts to system settings panels:\n    - Wi-Fi: `Settings.Panel.ACTION_WIFI` (or `Settings.ACTION_WIFI_SETTINGS`)\n    - Bluetooth: `Settings.ACTION_BLUETOOTH_SETTINGS`\n    - Location: `Settings.ACTION_LOCATION_SOURCE_SETTINGS`\n  - Explicit UI copy states: \"Opens system control panel to disable device radio antennas.\"\n\n### E. WhatsApp Relay\n- **OS Constraint**: WhatsApp does not expose an API for third-party apps to send messages in the background without user confirmation.\n- **Compliant Architectural Design**:\n  - Uses standard URI intent: `https://api.whatsapp.com/send?phone=+1234567890&text=...`.\n  - Disclosed as a manual one-tap user relay, never claiming automated background delivery.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Proposed Native Kotlin Project Structure\n\n```\napp/src/main/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AndroidManifest.xml\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 java/com/example/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 MainActivity.kt                      # Single activity, window insets, edge-to-edge\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CloakApplication.kt                  # Application class, DI/container initialization\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 core/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 audio/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AudioChunkRecorder.kt        # 5-second chunk recorder with MediaRecorder\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AudioFileManager.kt          # Temp file cleanup and retention\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 location/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LocationProvider.kt          # FusedLocationProviderClient wrapper\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 LocationFormatter.kt         # Maps URL builder & formatting\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 security/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CryptoManager.kt             # PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256, secure salt generation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 PinStorage.kt                # EncryptedSharedPreferences for PIN hashes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 sensor/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ShakeDetector.kt             # SensorEventListener for gravity-free spikes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 telephony/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SmsDispatcher.kt             # SmsManager native sender + intent fallback\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 WhatsAppRelay.kt             # wa.me intent launcher\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 data/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 local/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CloakDatabase.kt             # Room DB for contacts & period logs\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ContactDao.kt                # Support circle DAO\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PeriodDao.kt                 # Cycle logs DAO\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 entity/                      # EmergencyContact, PeriodEntry entities\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 network/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseConfig.kt            # Supabase URL & public anon key config\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseClient.kt            # OkHttp / Retrofit HTTP client for Supabase REST\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseSosRepository.kt     # sos_sessions & sos_locations API calls\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SupabaseStorageRepository.kt # Storage bucket audio uploads with retry\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 BurnerNoteRepository.kt      # read_and_burn RPC integration\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 repository/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ContactRepository.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 PeriodRepository.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 service/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 SosForegroundService.kt          # Audio & location foreground service\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ui/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 navigation/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Screen.kt                    # Type-safe navigation routes\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AppNavHost.kt                # Root Navigation host with BackHandler\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 theme/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Color.kt                     # M3 Color palette (Blush, Rose, Slate)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Theme.kt                     # Petal Material3 Theme\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Type.kt                      # Clean typography\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 KeypadScreen.kt              # Discreet 4-digit PIN pad\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PinSetupScreen.kt            # First-run Normal & Duress setup\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthViewModel.kt             # PIN verification & routing logic\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 tracker/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 TrackerMainScreen.kt         # Scaffold with Bottom Navigation\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 CalendarTab.kt               # Menstrual cycle calendar & predictions\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LogTab.kt                    # Symptom & mood chip logging\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 TipsTab.kt                   # 15 evidence-based wellness cards\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SettingsTab.kt               # Support circle contacts & preferences\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 FakeCallScreen.kt            # \"Call Gynecologist\" incoming call UI\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 TrackerViewModel.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 shield/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ShieldDashboardScreen.kt     # Secret 3-tile dashboard\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 PhotoSanitizerScreen.kt      # EXIF strip, photo picker, save clean copy\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DigitalLockdownScreen.kt     # Radio toggle deep-links\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 BurnerNotesScreen.kt         # Ephemeral note writer & code retriever\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ShieldViewModel.kt\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 fakesleep/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 FakeSleepOverlay.kt          # Black screen with 3s hold-to-unlock\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 util/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ExifStripper.kt                  # ExifInterface cleaner & JPEG re-encoder\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 GestureExtensions.kt             # 3-second hold with pixel threshold detector\n```\n\n### Gradle & Dependency Plan (`app/build.gradle.kts`)\n- **AndroidX & Jetpack Compose**: Compose BOM, Material3, Navigation Compose, Lifecycle Runtime Compose.\n- **Room Persistence**: `androidx.room:room-runtime`, `androidx.room:room-ktx`, `androidx.room:room-compiler` (KSP).\n- **Networking & JSON**: `com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp`, `com.squareup.retrofit2:retrofit`, `com.squareup.moshi:moshi-kotlin`.\n- **Hardware & Sensors**: Native `android.hardware.SensorManager`, `com.google.android.gms:play-services-location`.\n- **Media & EXIF**: `androidx.exifinterface:exifinterface`.\n- **Testing**: JUnit4, Robolectric 4.14+, Compose UI Test, Kotlin Coroutines Test.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Required Android Permissions & Justifications\n\n| Permission | Protection Level | Functional Justification |\n|------------|------------------|--------------------------|\n| `android.permission.INTERNET` | Normal | Uploading SOS audio chunks, persisting SOS locations, and communicating with Supabase REST API / Burner Notes. |\n| `android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE` | Normal | Detecting active internet connectivity to trigger offline queue retries. |\n| `android.permission.VIBRATE` | Normal | Providing subtle haptic feedback for the 3-second hidden Shield gesture and keypad interactions. |\n| `android.permission.SEND_SMS` | Dangerous | Sending urgent SOS alerts with GPS coordinates to Support Circle contacts during duress or shake trigger. |\n| `android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION` | Dangerous | Acquiring high-accuracy GPS coordinates for emergency SMS and live tracking updates. |\n| `android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION` | Dangerous | Fallback approximate cell/Wi-Fi location when GPS lock is slow or indoors. |\n| `android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO` | Dangerous | Capturing 5-second audio evidence chunks during an active SOS emergency session. |\n| `android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE` | Normal | Running the uninterrupted SOS safety session when the screen is dimmed or Fake-Sleep is active. |\n| `android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MICROPHONE` | Normal | Mandated by Android 14+ for recording audio from a background service. |\n| `android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION` | Normal | Mandated by Android 14+ for streaming location fixes during an active SOS service. |\n| `android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS` | Dangerous (API 33+) | Displaying the system-required persistent notification for foreground service operation. |\n| `android.permission.WAKE_LOCK` | Normal | Keeping the CPU active to prevent the device from entering deep sleep during Fake-Sleep audio upload. |\n\n*Note: For the Photo Sanitizer, modern zero-permission Android Photo Picker (`ActivityResultContracts.PickVisualMedia`) and `MediaStore` Scoped Storage will be used, eliminating the need for broad storage permissions (`READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE`).*\n\n---\n\n## 6. Supabase Backend Architecture & Schema Plan\n\n### A. SQL Schema & Row Level Security (RLS)\n\n```sql\n-- 1. SOS SESSIONS TABLE\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.sos_sessions (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    session_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    trigger_source TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (trigger_source IN (\'duress_pin\', \'shake\', \'manual_test\')),\n    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \'active\' CHECK (status IN (\'active\', \'resolved\', \'cancelled\')),\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT timezone(\'utc\', now()),\n    ended_at TIMESTAMPTZ\n);\n\nALTER TABLE public.sos_sessions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- Allow anonymous client to insert sessions (write-only)\nCREATE POLICY \"Allow anon insert to sos_sessions\" \nON public.sos_sessions FOR INSERT \nTO anon WITH CHECK (true);\n\n-- Deny public reading of all SOS sessions\nCREATE POLICY \"Deny anon select to sos_sessions\" \nON public.sos_sessions FOR SELECT \nTO anon USING (false);\n\n-- 2. SOS LOCATIONS TABLE\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.sos_locations (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    session_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES public.sos_sessions(session_id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    latitude DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,\n    longitude DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,\n    accuracy REAL,\n    recorded_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT timezone(\'utc\', now())\n);\n\nALTER TABLE public.sos_locations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Allow anon insert to sos_locations\" \nON public.sos_locations FOR INSERT \nTO anon WITH CHECK (true);\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Deny anon select to sos_locations\" \nON public.sos_locations FOR SELECT \nTO anon USING (false);\n\n-- 3. BURNER NOTES TABLE\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.burner_notes (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    access_code TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    note_body TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT timezone(\'utc\', now()),\n    expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT (timezone(\'utc\', now()) + INTERVAL \'24 hours\')\n);\n\nALTER TABLE public.burner_notes ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- Clients can insert a note with code\nCREATE POLICY \"Allow anon insert to burner_notes\" \nON public.burner_notes FOR INSERT \nTO anon WITH CHECK (char_length(access_code) = 6);\n\n-- Clients cannot directly query or list burner_notes table\nCREATE POLICY \"Deny direct anon select to burner_notes\" \nON public.burner_notes FOR SELECT \nTO anon USING (false);\n\n-- 4. ATOMIC READ-AND-BURN DATABASE FUNCTION\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.read_and_burn(p_code TEXT)\nRETURNS TABLE (note_content TEXT, is_valid BOOLEAN)\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n    v_note_body TEXT;\nBEGIN\n    -- Delete and return in a single atomic transaction\n    DELETE FROM public.burner_notes\n    WHERE access_code = p_code\n      AND expires_at > timezone(\'utc\', now())\n    RETURNING note_body INTO v_note_body;\n\n    IF v_note_body IS NOT NULL THEN\n        RETURN QUERY SELECT v_note_body AS note_content, true AS is_valid;\n    ELSE\n        RETURN QUERY SELECT NULL::TEXT AS note_content, false AS is_valid;\n    END IF;\nEND;\n$$;\n\n-- 5. STORAGE BUCKET CONFIGURATION\n-- Bucket: \'sos_audio\' (Private)\n-- Policy: Anon role can upload files into their own session prefix: session_id/*\n-- Policy: Anon cannot list or download files from the bucket\n```\n\n### B. Client Security Policy\n- The Android client will only use the public **Anon Key** and **Project URL**, injected via `.env` / `BuildConfig`.\n- Under no circumstances will a service-role key or master database credential be included in the APK.\n- All writes are blind inserts into RLS-protected tables; reads are strictly prohibited except via the atomic `read_and_burn` RPC function.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Windows Setup, Build, & PowerShell Test Commands\n\nThe user\'s project location is `D:\\CloakNative`. Below are the exact Windows PowerShell commands:\n\n### A. Environment Verification\n```powershell\n# Verify Java 17+ and Git\njava -version\ngit --version\n```\n\n### B. Project Setup & Validation (in `D:\\CloakNative`)\n```powershell\nSet-Location -Path \"D:\\CloakNative\"\n\n# Check Gradle status and clean state\ngradle --version\n```\n\n### C. Build & Compile Test\n```powershell\n# Compile the native debug APK\ngradle :app:assembleDebug\n```\n\n### D. Unit & Robolectric Test Execution\n```powershell\n# Run all unit and JVM-based Robolectric tests with detailed test report\ngradle :app:testDebugUnitTest --info\n```\n\n### E. Install on Connected Real Device / Emulator\n```powershell\n# Install debug build on connected Android device via ADB\nadb devices\ngradle :app:installDebug\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Feasibility & Implementation Classification\n\n### A. Fully Implementable in Native Android & Automated Testable\n1. Cryptographic PIN derivation (PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256), salt generator, and constant-time verifier.\n2. Custom 4-digit keypad UI, auto-submit, backspace, and masking.\n3. Centralized idempotent SOS state engine with event emission (`SosState.Idle`, `SosState.Active`, `SosState.Stopped`).\n4. Fake-Sleep UI overlay, 15s countdown timer, and 3-second hold gesture detector.\n5. Menstrual cycle calculations, 28-day prediction algorithm, symptom chip states, and 15 wellness cards.\n6. \"Call Gynecologist\" incoming call UI simulation with custom caller name.\n7. Hidden 3-second logo press with 20px movement cancellation and background auto-dismissal.\n8. Photo Sanitizer EXIF stripper removing all GPS/device tags and verifying output stream.\n9. Room database persistence for emergency contacts and local cycle logs.\n10. Supabase REST payloads and atomic `read_and_burn` RPC consumer.\n\n### B. Requires Real Device Testing\n1. **Physical Accelerometer Shake Detection**: Validating the 3-spike $\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ threshold under real-world movement (walking, sitting, pocket movement vs. intentional vigorous shake).\n2. **Native SMS Dispatch**: Verification with real cellular SIM carrier, handling airplane mode, unprovisioned SIM, and signal loss.\n3. **Hardware GPS Fix**: Verifying transition from last known location to high-precision satellite fix indoors vs. outdoors.\n4. **Haptic Vibration**: Physical tactile feel of the short vibration confirming secret Shield entry.\n\n### C. Android Platform Constraints & Safe Behaviors\n1. **Background Microphone Recording**: Must use a Foreground Service started while the app is active; Android OS displays a privacy indicator dot.\n2. **Silent Radio Toggling**: Android restricts third-party apps from silently toggling Wi-Fi/Bluetooth; the app provides one-tap system setting panel shortcuts.\n3. **Automated WhatsApp Dispatch**: WhatsApp has no silent send API; implemented as a direct pre-filled `wa.me` intent.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Stage Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n### Stage 1: Project Foundation & Secure PIN\n- [ ] Native Kotlin Jetpack Compose project compiles cleanly with zero warnings/errors.\n- [ ] First-run wizard prompts user to set Normal PIN and Duress PIN (rejects identical PINs).\n- [ ] Salted PBKDF2 hash stored securely; constant-time comparison prevents timing attacks.\n- [ ] Custom 4-digit keypad unlocks into the disguise tracker for both PINs.\n- [ ] Entering Duress PIN triggers `SosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")` in background.\n- [ ] Normal PIN verifies without triggering SOS.\n\n### Stage 2: Core SOS, Contacts, Location, & SMS\n- [ ] Support Circle screen allows adding, viewing, and deleting up to 3 emergency contacts in Room DB.\n- [ ] `ShakeDetector` reliably identifies 3 acceleration spikes ($\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart within $1.5\\,\\text{s}$).\n- [ ] Central SOS state machine is idempotent: duplicate triggers do not cause multiple simultaneous dispatches.\n- [ ] Native SMS sent via `SmsManager` with Google Maps link: `https://maps.google.com/?q=LAT,LNG`.\n- [ ] Fallback to last known location first, transitioning to fresh location updates every ~2 minutes.\n- [ ] Entering Normal PIN stops active SOS; Duress PIN keeps SOS active while returning to tracker.\n\n### Stage 3: Audio Chunks, Supabase Upload, & Fake-Sleep\n- [ ] `SosForegroundService` captures audio in ~5-second AAC chunks with ongoing notification.\n- [ ] Audio chunks uploaded to Supabase Storage bucket with exponential backoff on network failure.\n- [ ] SOS session status and location stream logged in `sos_sessions` and `sos_locations`.\n- [ ] After 15 seconds of inactivity during active SOS, screen goes completely black (Fake-Sleep).\n- [ ] 3-second continuous hold on Fake-Sleep reveals PIN keypad.\n- [ ] Normal PIN exits Fake-Sleep and stops SOS; Duress PIN returns to tracker while maintaining SOS.\n\n### Stage 4: Public Disguise Tracker & Simulated Call\n- [ ] Calendar displays marked period days, predicted next cycle days, and symptom dots.\n- [ ] Symptom chips and mood selection persist to local database.\n- [ ] Scrolling Tips screen renders 15 evidence-based women\'s health cards.\n- [ ] \"Call Gynecologist\" card launches realistic incoming phone call screen.\n- [ ] Normal tap displays \"Mom\"; long press displays \"Police\"; ringtone plays with graceful fallback.\n\n### Stage 5: Digital Shield\n- [ ] 3-second hold on top-left logo with $< 20\\,\\text{px}$ movement triggers haptic pulse and opens Shield.\n- [ ] Shield gesture is locked out while SOS is active.\n- [ ] Shield automatically dismisses to root tracker when app is backgrounded (`ON_STOP`).\n- [ ] Photo Sanitizer strips all EXIF tags (GPS, camera model, date) and verifies clean output.\n- [ ] Digital Lockdown shortcuts open system panels for Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and Location.\n- [ ] Burner Notes creates note with 6-digit code; atomic RPC deletes note upon first retrieval; second attempt confirms destruction.\n\n### Stage 6: Hardening, Release Build, & 90-Second Demo\n- [ ] All unit and Robolectric tests pass (`gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`).\n- [ ] Release APK built without warnings (`gradle :app:assembleRelease`).\n- [ ] End-to-end verification report documenting verified vs. platform-constrained features.\n- [ ] 90-second clear demo script prepared.\n\n---\n\n**Stage 0 is complete. Awaiting your approval before proceeding to Stage 1.**"
