  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Begin Implementation**\n\nI\'ve moved past Stage 0 planning and am initiating Stage 1. My focus is on inspecting the project workspace and available tools. Currently, I\'m concentrated on the D:\\Clo directory and the file-editing and build capabilities to begin this stage.\n\n\n**Refine Stage 1 Details**\n\nI\'m solidifying the specifications for Stage 1. I\'m focusing on the native Android foundation, especially its core safety engine elements: project structure, Compose theme, and state management. The tracker shell, PIN keypad (normal/duress), and first-run setup flow are being refined. I\'m also ensuring the duress PIN triggers the SOS controller correctly, all while avoiding hardcoded demo PINs.\n\n\n**Detail Security Measures**\n\nI\'m now incorporating security measures. I\'m focusing on PIN verification with PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256, random salts, and constant-time verification. I am avoiding plaintext PIN storage and fast hashes. I am also detailing the emergency contact system with management and permission states, and the SOS controller, which will centralize and maintain the SOS state, recording its trigger source. I am working on foreground shake detection and location services for emergency SMS, including Google Maps URLs. The SMS process will use native Android `SmsManager` and will provide support up to 3 emergency contacts.\n\n\n"
