  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Security Modules**\n\nI\'m currently focused on planning the architectural modules for Stage 1. Specifically, I\'m thinking through the `com.example.core.security.CryptoManager` module, and I plan to use PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256 with iterations in the 10,000 to 100,000 range and a 32-byte key length (256 bits). I also want it to generate a random 16-byte salt.\n\n\n**Refining Crypto Details**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the `CryptoManager` module, making sure it handles PIN hashing securely. I\'m using `SecureRandom` for salt generation, with a focus on Base64 encoding. I have a plan for constant-time comparisons with `MessageDigest.isEqual(...)`, and I\'ve started thinking about `PinStorage`, and the distinction between normal and duress PINs.\n\n\n\n**Designing Sensor Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating sensor-based shake detection, focusing on the `ShakeDetector` class. I\'ve defined how it listens for accelerometer data and calculates gravity-free acceleration. The spike detection logic includes thresholds, intervals, and window durations to trigger callbacks. I\'ve also implemented a helper method for unit testing the logic.\n\n\n**Implementing Emergency Dispatch**\n\nI\'m now implementing the emergency SMS dispatch functionality using `SmsManager` within `telephony.SmsDispatcher`. I\'ve added a check for `SEND_SMS` permission and am working on supporting up to three contacts. I\'m building the message with a Maps URL, including error handling for exceptions, missing contacts, and SIM issues. There\'s also a fallback method using `Intent.ACTION_SENDTO`.\n\n**Integrating Location Services**\n\nI\'m integrating location services, leveraging `FusedLocationProviderClient` within `LocationProvider`. I\'ve implemented methods for retrieving the last known location and a high-accuracy fresh location, formatting the Google Maps URL for easy sharing.\n\n**Establishing SOS Controller States**\n\nI\'m designing a central idempotent SOS controller, with state management that incorporates: Idle, Active (with a session ID, trigger source, start time, and last known location and update timestamp), and a final Cancelled state. This will be a Singleton or shared repository/controller.\n\n\n**Orchestrating SOS Actions**\n\nI\'m working on the `SosController` methods. The `startSos()` method is idempotent, ensuring duplicate SMS dispatches don\'t occur. I generate a `sessionId`, obtain the last location, and dispatch SMS to contacts. A periodic coroutine loop updates the location every 2 minutes. The `stopSos()` method transitions the state and cancels the loop. I\'ve also implemented methods to check the active state and access it via a StateFlow. I\'m focusing on seamless PIN integration, using normal and duress PINs for activation and deactivation.\n\n\n**Developing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on the UI layer, specifically the PIN setup and keypad screens. The `PinSetupScreen` handles the first-run wizard, ensuring normal and duress PINs are created and validated, preventing identical PINs. The `KeypadScreen` features a custom 4-digit keypad with masked input and haptic feedback. There is also an error shake animation for incorrect entries. Finally, the `TrackerShellScreen` provides a discreet disguise and handles emergency contacts management.\n\n\n"
