  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Sensor ShakeDetector**\n\nI\'m now diving into building the `ShakeDetector`. The prompt directs me to leverage Android\'s gravity-free accelerometer data. The core challenge involves detecting three qualifying acceleration spikes, spaced at least 250 milliseconds apart, within a 1.5-second window. I\'m focusing on crafting the spike detection logic first.\n\n\n**Refining Shake Detector Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `ShakeDetector.kt` class. I\'ve defined configurable parameters: threshold, spike intervals, window duration, and required spikes. I\'m registering a `SensorEventListener` for accelerometer data and implementing a high-pass gravity filter. The plan is to maintain a timestamp queue for qualifying spikes and remove those outside the window duration. My current focus is implementing the logic for identifying and tracking these spikes, considering the time constraints.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_497798"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.core.sensor\\n\\nimport android.content.Context\\nimport android.hardware.Sensor\\nimport android.hardware.SensorEvent\\nimport android.hardware.SensorEventListener\\nimport android.hardware.SensorManager\\nimport kotlin.math.sqrt\\n\\n/**\\n * Detects deliberate shake gestures using gravity-free linear acceleration.\\n * Requirements:\\n * - 3 qualifying acceleration spikes >= threshold (default 18.0 m/s^2)\\n * - Each spike separated by >= 250ms\\n * - All 3 spikes within a 1.5-second (1500ms) sliding window\\n * - Exclusively foreground operation\\n */\\nclass ShakeDetector(\\n  private val context: Context,\\n  var threshold: Float = DEFAULT_THRESHOLD,\\n  val minSpikeIntervalMs: Long = DEFAULT_MIN_SPIKE_INTERVAL_MS,\\n  val windowDurationMs: Long = DEFAULT_WINDOW_MS,\\n  val requiredSpikes: Int = DEFAULT_REQUIRED_SPIKES,\\n  private val onShakeTriggered: () -> Unit\\n) : SensorEventListener {\\n\\n  companion object {\\n    const val DEFAULT_THRESHOLD = 18.0f // m/s^2\\n    const val DEFAULT_MIN_SPIKE_INTERVAL_MS = 250L\\n    const val DEFAULT_WINDOW_MS = 1500L\\n    const val DEFAULT_REQUIRED_SPIKES = 3\\n    private const val GRAVITY_ALPHA = 0.8f\\n    private const val COOLDOWN_MS = 2000L\\n  }\\n\\n  private var sensorManager: SensorManager? = null\\n  private var accelerometer: Sensor? = null\\n  private var isListening = false\\n\\n  // High-pass filter gravity components\\n  private val gravity = FloatArray(3)\\n  private val spikeTimestamps = mutableListOf<Long>()\\n  private var lastTriggerTimestamp = 0L\\n\\n  fun start() {\\n    if (isListening) return\\n    sensorManager = context.getSystemService(Context.SENSOR_SERVICE) as? SensorManager\\n    accelerometer = sensorManager?.getDefaultSensor(Sensor.TYPE_ACCELEROMETER)\\n    accelerometer?.let {\\n      sensorManager?.registerListener(this, it, SensorManager.SENSOR_DELAY_GAME)\\n      isListening = true\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  fun stop() {\\n    if (!isListening) return\\n    sensorManager?.unregisterListener(this)\\n    isListening = false\\n    spikeTimestamps.clear()\\n  }\\n\\n  override fun onSensorChanged(event: SensorEvent?) {\\n    if (event == null || event.sensor.type != Sensor.TYPE_ACCELEROMETER) return\\n\\n    val now = System.currentTimeMillis()\\n\\n    // 1. Isolate gravity using low-pass filter\\n    gravity[0] = GRAVITY_ALPHA * gravity[0] + (1 - GRAVITY_ALPHA) * event.values[0]\\n    gravity[1] = GRAVITY_ALPHA * gravity[1] + (1 - GRAVITY_ALPHA) * event.values[1]\\n    gravity[2] = GRAVITY_ALPHA * gravity[2] + (1 - GRAVITY_ALPHA) * event.values[2]\\n\\n    // 2. Remove gravity to get linear acceleration\\n    val linearX = event.values[0] - gravity[0]\\n    val linearY = event.values[1] - gravity[1]\\n    val linearZ = event.values[2] - gravity[2]\\n\\n    val linearMagnitude = sqrt((linearX * linearX + linearY * linearY + linearZ * linearZ).toDouble()).toFloat()\\n\\n    val triggered = processAccelerationSample(linearMagnitude, now)\\n    if (triggered) {\\n      onShakeTriggered()\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  override fun onAccuracyChanged(sensor: Sensor?, accuracy: Int) {}\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Process a single acceleration magnitude sample against the window and interval rules.\\n   * Public for deterministic unit testing without requiring real hardware.\\n   */\\n  fun processAccelerationSample(magnitude: Float, timestampMs: Long): Boolean {\\n    // Check refractory cooldown\\n    if (timestampMs - lastTriggerTimestamp < COOLDOWN_MS) {\\n      return false\\n    }\\n\\n    // Prune spikes outside the sliding window\\n    spikeTimestamps.removeAll { timestampMs - it > windowDurationMs }\\n\\n    if (magnitude >= threshold) {\\n      val lastSpike = spikeTimestamps.lastOrNull()\\n      if (lastSpike == null || (timestampMs - lastSpike) >= minSpikeIntervalMs) {\\n        spikeTimestamps.add(timestampMs)\\n\\n        if (spikeTimestamps.size >= requiredSpikes) {\\n          spikeTimestamps.clear()\\n          lastTriggerTimestamp = timestampMs\\n          return true\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    return false\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Implement gravity-free ShakeDetector with configurable threshold and testable processing engine\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/core/sensor/ShakeDetector.kt\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing ShakeDetector\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create ShakeDetector.kt\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\376\020\n\373\020\001i\024}\023\277m\240-\263\240\206Mz\275)\303 \037j8\222\241\304\364\'q\203\034P4U\233-f\202\326.Gi\353\363\237\226j\320Q\315V\352\305F!3\277\230\317\201\035\324\306`I%\254QY)\247\231\247L/\265hl\036D\241\030\236\247\345\326;\355V9\f\227\356^\203p/T\272\274\241\251\373\370\\\322\365\035\226(\354(\365&E\364\026\353\3637\352\254f\017\243\200\310\337\033\035\317m\202\020u\221g\n\024\211\305\313\323\232\363\334\037+\240BN>~/Z\210;Gn\374\367\200\317:\225M\377 F\362\273\3028\024\034W_ \353\366|K\360\3140:g\030Ir\203B\344\277#i\263\372\260\323Q\347\262\363\336\023/&t\376\366\f\"-\030\366EX\237\323\302\244\266\266eM\022\271d\377\344\342r\024N_\023b\237\257;\312\233\210\244:\257\266\274\315\323\211_\347A\032\033\374\353\224M\031m\275f\214\0254\3441\275=z\321\314\201[M\201\341\002\213H+\333\273H\034\'\230\337m*\275\263\031\v\220\271\322c\022,\253\276+MdD\003\206\222\337`P\017\334\336{o\344cu\333``-t\234\242\351\\38\241\002\254\320z\372\f\036\344\310\247\244*\371T\342p\032N\333\025\263\207w\316\031\250\341\213\244\330\336\275\224\303\342\016\313%l&\263\300z\344\032\"\022\324\224|\272\377\306g\3152\324\257/E\361\027x\333\265\365\262\210\257\177I\023\2350\350s\276\331\212\277Q5\3141\034\024\325\362\355\263\253Z\266\001d\313W\333\376\004?\311Q\3714\035\367\261\360V\003\006\361\036lm\331{\305F\017\265 P\237\253\375[ID\'\347e\a\36179\260\230b\364Hr\247\377\266^\2765\344>%0&\2750\262\303w\002\2357\b2Q\005\311\255\a\315\307\003) \345*\316@\325\330\354tS\221\277\036\276\336\337\211\326\346\340!/\342+\266\313s~4q\237\005H0\355b\206%g~(\315\300\260\210~5,\306;\317N\307@\277\3240\240\262ps\031\312XZ\340\326fM\022\366\241\017_\234+E\312K\320\346\204v\213okd\005\277\202~~|+]3\344bg\207\212\342\313K\021g\354\315H)\224\031\352+\177&|\017\201\v\n\360vk\331\371j\177\b\023\201`n\252\212\265\354\305&\204\305\361\215\273\2407w\352\223E\305\r\337\303\213\253\307G\355\327\346\305\210:\276\344\261\275\345\334\273^Ca\331\302\250\317;\021>)@\2514a\320