  planner_response {
    response: "# STAGE 1 REPORT: NATIVE FOUNDATION + CORE SAFETY ENGINE\n\n## 1. Stage Status\n**Complete and Verified.**\nThe native Android foundation, cryptographic PIN derivation engine, custom keypad, dual PIN routing, Support Circle Room database, gravity-free linear acceleration shake detector, and central idempotent SOS controller have been built and verified via compilation and passing unit/Robolectric test suites.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files Created or Modified\n\n### Core Architecture & Configuration\n- `/metadata.json` \342\200\224 Configured platform identity for Petal with preserved server-side capabilities.\n- `/settings.gradle.kts` \342\200\224 Set root project name to `Cloak`.\n- `/app/build.gradle.kts` \342\200\224 Set unique `applicationId` (`com.aistudio.cloak.vzkpmn`), enabled `navigation-compose`, `room`, `play-services-location`, `coil-compose`, and `exifinterface`.\n- `/gradle/libs.versions.toml` \342\200\224 Added `androidx-exifinterface` library dependency.\n- `/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml` \342\200\224 Configured public launcher label `\"Petal\"`.\n- `/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` \342\200\224 Declared `CloakApplication`, hardware sensors (`accelerometer`), and required permissions (`SEND_SMS`, `ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`, `RECORD_AUDIO`, `FOREGROUND_SERVICE`, `VIBRATE`, `INTERNET`).\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/CloakApplication.kt` \342\200\224 Application container orchestrating the singleton lifecycle for database, repositories, sensor listener, and SOS controller.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt` \342\200\224 Edge-to-edge entry point binding foreground sensor detection to activity resume/pause.\n\n### Security & Hardware Engine (`com.example.core`)\n- `core/security/CryptoManager.kt` \342\200\224 Cryptographic engine implementing `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256` (10,000 iterations, 256-bit key) with 16-byte random salting and constant-time comparison (`MessageDigest.isEqual`) to eliminate timing-channel vulnerabilities.\n- `core/security/PinStorage.kt` \342\200\224 Secure storage and independent verification channels for Normal and Duress credentials, enforcing 4-digit numeric validation and distinct values.\n- `core/sensor/ShakeDetector.kt` \342\200\224 Gravity-free linear accelerometer processor detecting 3 qualifying acceleration spikes ($\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$) spaced $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart within a $1500\\,\\text{ms}$ window.\n- `core/location/LocationProvider.kt` \342\200\224 Location service wrapper prioritizing cached last-known coordinates with fresh high-accuracy fallback and Google Maps URL builder (`https://maps.google.com/?q=LAT,LNG`).\n- `core/telephony/SmsDispatcher.kt` \342\200\224 Native `SmsManager` multipart SMS dispatcher with exception isolation and fallback composer intent.\n- `core/sos/SosState.kt` & `core/sos/SosController.kt` \342\200\224 Centralized, idempotent SOS state machine coordinating Duress PIN and Shake triggers, dispatching emergency SMS, and scheduling periodic updates (~2 minutes).\n\n### Local Persistence & UI (`com.example.data` & `com.example.ui`)\n- `data/local/entity/EmergencyContact.kt` \342\200\224 Room entity for Support Circle contacts.\n- `data/local/dao/ContactDao.kt` \342\200\224 Contact DAO with query, insert, and delete operations.\n- `data/local/CloakDatabase.kt` \342\200\224 Room Database instance.\n- `data/repository/ContactRepository.kt` \342\200\224 Repository enforcing a maximum limit of 3 emergency contacts.\n- `ui/theme/Color.kt` & `ui/theme/Theme.kt` \342\200\224 Disguise palette (Soft Rose, Warm Blush, Deep Slate) for Petal.\n- `ui/navigation/Screen.kt` & `ui/navigation/AppNavHost.kt` \342\200\224 Navigation graph with BackHandler protection preventing PIN bypass.\n- `ui/auth/KeypadScreen.kt` \342\200\224 Custom 4-digit keypad with masked dots, haptic feedback, and auto-submit.\n- `ui/auth/PinSetupScreen.kt` \342\200\224 First-run onboarding wizard with validation, error states, and architecture demo preset loader (1234 / 9999).\n- `ui/tracker/TrackerShellScreen.kt` \342\200\224 Disguise tracker shell containing cycle indicators, Support Circle contact management, permission requests, and live SOS diagnostic monitors.\n\n### Automated Test Suite\n- `app/src/test/java/com/example/Stage1SafetyEngineTest.kt` \342\200\224 Comprehensive unit and Robolectric tests covering PBKDF2 salting, PIN validation, duress separation, shake detector mathematical filtering, and SOS state idempotency.\n- `app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleRobolectricTest.kt` \342\200\224 Updated to verify the localized app name `\"Petal\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact PowerShell Build & Test Commands\n\nTo build and execute tests for the project in `D:\\CloakNative`:\n\n```powershell\nSet-Location -Path \"D:\\CloakNative\"\n\n# 1. Compile the debug APK\ngradle :app:assembleDebug\n\n# 2. Run unit and Robolectric tests with test logs\ngradle :app:testDebugUnitTest --info\n\n# 3. Install on connected test device via ADB\nadb install -r app\\build\\outputs\\apk\\debug\\app-debug.apk\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tests Actually Run & Actual Results\n\nCommand executed:\n`gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`\n\n**Output:**\n```\nTask :app:compileDebugKotlin\nTask :app:compileDebugUnitTestKotlin\nTask :app:testDebugUnitTest\n\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > cryptoManager_hashesPinWithRandomSaltAndVerifiesCorrectly PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_rejectsInvalidLengthOrIdenticalPins PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_distinguishesNormalAndDuressCredentials PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_identifiesThreeSpikesWithProperSpacing PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_ignoresNormalWalkingMovementBelowThreshold PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > sosController_idempotentDuressTriggerAndNormalStop PASSED\nExampleUnitTest > addition_isCorrect PASSED\nExampleRobolectricTest > read string from context PASSED\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 37s\n33 actionable tasks: 7 executed, 26 up-to-date\n```\n\n**Compilation Check:**\n`compile_applet` executed and returned: **Build succeeded - the applet is compiled.**\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verified Features vs. Platform Limitations\n\n### Verified in Host Environment\n- **Cryptographic Separation**: PBKDF2 random salting produces distinct hashes for identical inputs; constant-time byte comparison prevents timing analysis.\n- **PIN Setup & Storage**: Enforces 4 numeric digits and rejects identical Normal and Duress credentials.\n- **Dual PIN Routing**: Keypad silently starts `SosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")` on Duress PIN and stops SOS on Normal PIN; both transition to the exact same disguise screen.\n- **Idempotency**: Repeated triggers (duress re-entry or shake while active) do not spawn duplicate sessions or alter the active session UUID.\n- **Shake Detection Math**: Mathematical verification confirms rejection of walking vibrations ($< 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$), rejection of rapid vibrations ($< 250\\,\\text{ms}$), and trigger confirmation upon 3 qualifying spikes within $1500\\,\\text{ms}$.\n- **Support Circle Limit**: Contact repository enforces the 3-contact ceiling.\n\n### Real-Device / Hardware Limitations\n- **Cellular Carrier & SIM**: Actual SMS dispatch requires a physical Android device with an activated SIM card. If permissions are granted but no SIM is inserted or mobile signal is unavailable, `SmsDispatcher` safely catches the error without crashing.\n- **Background Sensor Lifecycle**: In compliance with Android OS battery optimization and background restrictions, shake detection operates while the app is in the foreground.\n\n---\n\n## 6. How to Back Up the Working Code\n\nRun the following in PowerShell to create an isolated timestamped backup of the verified Stage 1 state:\n\n```powershell\n$timestamp = Get-Date -Format \"yyyyMMdd_HHmmss\"\n$backupPath = \"D:\\CloakNative_Stage1_Backup_$timestamp\"\nCopy-Item -Path \"D:\\CloakNative\" -Destination $backupPath -Recurse -Exclude @(\".gradle\", \"build\", \".idea\")\nWrite-Host \"Stage 1 backup created at $backupPath\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Next Action Required\n\nStage 1 is complete and tested. \n\nPlease approve proceeding to **Stage 2 (Complete Disguise + Guardian Experience)** to implement:\n1. Full Menstrual Calendar (period days marked in red, predicted cycle in pink, symptom dots).\n2. Symptom and mood chip logging.\n3. 15 evidence-based wellness tip cards.\n4. \"Call Gynecologist\" incoming call simulator (Mom on tap, Police on long-press, ringtone + fallback).\n5. Foreground audio recorder (~5s chunks), Supabase upload pipeline with retry handling, and Supabase SQL migrations/RLS.\n6. Fake-Sleep 15-second inactivity blackout screen with 3-second hold-and-PIN unlock."
    modified_response: "# STAGE 1 REPORT: NATIVE FOUNDATION + CORE SAFETY ENGINE\n\n## 1. Stage Status\n**Complete and Verified.**\nThe native Android foundation, cryptographic PIN derivation engine, custom keypad, dual PIN routing, Support Circle Room database, gravity-free linear acceleration shake detector, and central idempotent SOS controller have been built and verified via compilation and passing unit/Robolectric test suites.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Files Created or Modified\n\n### Core Architecture & Configuration\n- `/metadata.json` \342\200\224 Configured platform identity for Petal with preserved server-side capabilities.\n- `/settings.gradle.kts` \342\200\224 Set root project name to `Cloak`.\n- `/app/build.gradle.kts` \342\200\224 Set unique `applicationId` (`com.aistudio.cloak.vzkpmn`), enabled `navigation-compose`, `room`, `play-services-location`, `coil-compose`, and `exifinterface`.\n- `/gradle/libs.versions.toml` \342\200\224 Added `androidx-exifinterface` library dependency.\n- `/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml` \342\200\224 Configured public launcher label `\"Petal\"`.\n- `/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` \342\200\224 Declared `CloakApplication`, hardware sensors (`accelerometer`), and required permissions (`SEND_SMS`, `ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`, `RECORD_AUDIO`, `FOREGROUND_SERVICE`, `VIBRATE`, `INTERNET`).\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/CloakApplication.kt` \342\200\224 Application container orchestrating the singleton lifecycle for database, repositories, sensor listener, and SOS controller.\n- `/app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt` \342\200\224 Edge-to-edge entry point binding foreground sensor detection to activity resume/pause.\n\n### Security & Hardware Engine (`com.example.core`)\n- `core/security/CryptoManager.kt` \342\200\224 Cryptographic engine implementing `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256` (10,000 iterations, 256-bit key) with 16-byte random salting and constant-time comparison (`MessageDigest.isEqual`) to eliminate timing-channel vulnerabilities.\n- `core/security/PinStorage.kt` \342\200\224 Secure storage and independent verification channels for Normal and Duress credentials, enforcing 4-digit numeric validation and distinct values.\n- `core/sensor/ShakeDetector.kt` \342\200\224 Gravity-free linear accelerometer processor detecting 3 qualifying acceleration spikes ($\\ge 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$) spaced $\\ge 250\\,\\text{ms}$ apart within a $1500\\,\\text{ms}$ window.\n- `core/location/LocationProvider.kt` \342\200\224 Location service wrapper prioritizing cached last-known coordinates with fresh high-accuracy fallback and Google Maps URL builder (`https://maps.google.com/?q=LAT,LNG`).\n- `core/telephony/SmsDispatcher.kt` \342\200\224 Native `SmsManager` multipart SMS dispatcher with exception isolation and fallback composer intent.\n- `core/sos/SosState.kt` & `core/sos/SosController.kt` \342\200\224 Centralized, idempotent SOS state machine coordinating Duress PIN and Shake triggers, dispatching emergency SMS, and scheduling periodic updates (~2 minutes).\n\n### Local Persistence & UI (`com.example.data` & `com.example.ui`)\n- `data/local/entity/EmergencyContact.kt` \342\200\224 Room entity for Support Circle contacts.\n- `data/local/dao/ContactDao.kt` \342\200\224 Contact DAO with query, insert, and delete operations.\n- `data/local/CloakDatabase.kt` \342\200\224 Room Database instance.\n- `data/repository/ContactRepository.kt` \342\200\224 Repository enforcing a maximum limit of 3 emergency contacts.\n- `ui/theme/Color.kt` & `ui/theme/Theme.kt` \342\200\224 Disguise palette (Soft Rose, Warm Blush, Deep Slate) for Petal.\n- `ui/navigation/Screen.kt` & `ui/navigation/AppNavHost.kt` \342\200\224 Navigation graph with BackHandler protection preventing PIN bypass.\n- `ui/auth/KeypadScreen.kt` \342\200\224 Custom 4-digit keypad with masked dots, haptic feedback, and auto-submit.\n- `ui/auth/PinSetupScreen.kt` \342\200\224 First-run onboarding wizard with validation, error states, and architecture demo preset loader (1234 / 9999).\n- `ui/tracker/TrackerShellScreen.kt` \342\200\224 Disguise tracker shell containing cycle indicators, Support Circle contact management, permission requests, and live SOS diagnostic monitors.\n\n### Automated Test Suite\n- `app/src/test/java/com/example/Stage1SafetyEngineTest.kt` \342\200\224 Comprehensive unit and Robolectric tests covering PBKDF2 salting, PIN validation, duress separation, shake detector mathematical filtering, and SOS state idempotency.\n- `app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleRobolectricTest.kt` \342\200\224 Updated to verify the localized app name `\"Petal\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exact PowerShell Build & Test Commands\n\nTo build and execute tests for the project in `D:\\CloakNative`:\n\n```powershell\nSet-Location -Path \"D:\\CloakNative\"\n\n# 1. Compile the debug APK\ngradle :app:assembleDebug\n\n# 2. Run unit and Robolectric tests with test logs\ngradle :app:testDebugUnitTest --info\n\n# 3. Install on connected test device via ADB\nadb install -r app\\build\\outputs\\apk\\debug\\app-debug.apk\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tests Actually Run & Actual Results\n\nCommand executed:\n`gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`\n\n**Output:**\n```\nTask :app:compileDebugKotlin\nTask :app:compileDebugUnitTestKotlin\nTask :app:testDebugUnitTest\n\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > cryptoManager_hashesPinWithRandomSaltAndVerifiesCorrectly PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_rejectsInvalidLengthOrIdenticalPins PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_distinguishesNormalAndDuressCredentials PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_identifiesThreeSpikesWithProperSpacing PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_ignoresNormalWalkingMovementBelowThreshold PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > sosController_idempotentDuressTriggerAndNormalStop PASSED\nExampleUnitTest > addition_isCorrect PASSED\nExampleRobolectricTest > read string from context PASSED\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 37s\n33 actionable tasks: 7 executed, 26 up-to-date\n```\n\n**Compilation Check:**\n`compile_applet` executed and returned: **Build succeeded - the applet is compiled.**\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verified Features vs. Platform Limitations\n\n### Verified in Host Environment\n- **Cryptographic Separation**: PBKDF2 random salting produces distinct hashes for identical inputs; constant-time byte comparison prevents timing analysis.\n- **PIN Setup & Storage**: Enforces 4 numeric digits and rejects identical Normal and Duress credentials.\n- **Dual PIN Routing**: Keypad silently starts `SosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")` on Duress PIN and stops SOS on Normal PIN; both transition to the exact same disguise screen.\n- **Idempotency**: Repeated triggers (duress re-entry or shake while active) do not spawn duplicate sessions or alter the active session UUID.\n- **Shake Detection Math**: Mathematical verification confirms rejection of walking vibrations ($< 18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$), rejection of rapid vibrations ($< 250\\,\\text{ms}$), and trigger confirmation upon 3 qualifying spikes within $1500\\,\\text{ms}$.\n- **Support Circle Limit**: Contact repository enforces the 3-contact ceiling.\n\n### Real-Device / Hardware Limitations\n- **Cellular Carrier & SIM**: Actual SMS dispatch requires a physical Android device with an activated SIM card. If permissions are granted but no SIM is inserted or mobile signal is unavailable, `SmsDispatcher` safely catches the error without crashing.\n- **Background Sensor Lifecycle**: In compliance with Android OS battery optimization and background restrictions, shake detection operates while the app is in the foreground.\n\n---\n\n## 6. How to Back Up the Working Code\n\nRun the following in PowerShell to create an isolated timestamped backup of the verified Stage 1 state:\n\n```powershell\n$timestamp = Get-Date -Format \"yyyyMMdd_HHmmss\"\n$backupPath = \"D:\\CloakNative_Stage1_Backup_$timestamp\"\nCopy-Item -Path \"D:\\CloakNative\" -Destination $backupPath -Recurse -Exclude @(\".gradle\", \"build\", \".idea\")\nWrite-Host \"Stage 1 backup created at $backupPath\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Next Action Required\n\nStage 1 is complete and tested. \n\nPlease approve proceeding to **Stage 2 (Complete Disguise + Guardian Experience)** to implement:\n1. Full Menstrual Calendar (period days marked in red, predicted cycle in pink, symptom dots).\n2. Symptom and mood chip logging.\n3. 15 evidence-based wellness tip cards.\n4. \"Call Gynecologist\" incoming call simulator (Mom on tap, Police on long-press, ringtone + fallback).\n5. Foreground audio recorder (~5s chunks), Supabase upload pipeline with retry handling, and Supabase SQL migrations/RLS.\n6. Fake-Sleep 15-second inactivity blackout screen with 3-second hold-and-PIN unlock."
