  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Current Stage**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the initial instructions and inventorying the existing, functional \"Stage 1\" components. The core directive is to craft \"Stage 2,\" which will involve a period tracker disguise alongside live SOS features. My immediate goal is to understand the established baseline before moving forward.\n\n\n**Analyzing Disguise Implementation**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the disguise aspect, specifically how the period tracker will function. \"Petal\" is the name, and I\'m designing the user interface around menstrual health themes. The calendar will be central, displaying cycle data, with log, tips, and settings sections. An incoming call card is planned with configurable contacts, including an SOS function. The emergency features will need seamless, accessible integration.\n\n\n**Defining Emergency Procedures**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in outlining the emergency procedures. It is critical the SOS feature is discreet, so no obvious button on the interface. I\'m focusing on defining workflows for PIN activation. My plan is for a support circle of up to three contacts with phone number validation. Live location sharing will send both the last known and fresh coordinates every two minutes. I\'ll need to clearly differentiate between the two in the SMS. In addition, I will be implementing audio recording, chunking it into 5-second increments and uploading them to a Supabase bucket. Finally, a black-screen interface is needed to help remain concealed.\n\n\n"
