  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Compilation Success**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the custom adaptive launcher icon and non-adaptive PNG icons compiled without a hitch! The next step involves a comprehensive inventory and planning of the remaining Stage 2 features. Currently, I\'m focusing on the \"Disguise Layer\" components, specifically the Period & Health Tracker\'s bottom section.\n\n\n**Defining Navigation Features**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the core navigation features. The calendar will be interactive, highlighting period days and predicted periods. I\'m designing the logging section with symptom chips, mood selection, and flow intensity options. Tips will be a scrolling view of evidence-based health cards. All data will persist locally to the Room database.\n\n\n**Outlining Safety Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing emergency contact settings (support circle up to 3) and cycle configuration (cycle length and period duration). Privacy options like PIN changes are also included. The \"Call Gynecologist\" card will have a simulated incoming call screen, and a long press triggers a simulated police call. I\'m focusing on the realistic interface, ringtone playback, and timer.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m making progress on Supabase integration and the audio chunk system. I\'ve set up the Supabase client using `.env` for security. I am designing the data models for SOS sessions, including session ID, trigger source, and status. I\'m also planning location records with latitude, longitude, and accuracy, and audio chunk metadata like sequence number, timestamp, and duration for storage.\n\n\n**Implementing SOS Mechanics**\n\nI\'m deep in the implementation of the SOS features now. The `AudioChunkRecorder` uses `MediaRecorder` to capture 5-second AAC chunks, and it dispatches each to `SupabaseStorageRepository` immediately, including a retry mechanism. I am building the `SosForegroundService` with a discreet notification, ensuring Android 14+ background microphone permission compliance. Also, I\'m designing a fake-sleep mode to preserve wake lock after 15 seconds of inactivity with a keypad recovery system.\n\n\n"
