  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Security Stages**\n\nOkay, I\'m now auditing the previous stages, focusing on the names, icons, and features. I\'m checking the Petal launcher, period-tracker icon, and the Calendar, Log, Tips, and Settings components. I\'m also confirming the normal and duress PINs. I\'m making sure everything aligns as specified.\n\n\n**Adding Emergency Features**\n\nI\'ve been adding emergency features: emergency contacts, shake-to-SOS, and SMS location sharing. I\'m implementing periodic location refreshes and short audio chunks with Supabase uploads. Also, I\'m working on the fake-sleep black screen and PIN recovery.\n\nI\'m also considering how to integrate a digital shield, with a hidden activation method. I\'m focusing on the technical aspects and making sure the user interface stays discreet, to avoid unwanted attention.\n\nFinally, I\'m integrating a photo EXIF sanitizer to strip sensitive information from user photos, by re-encoding the images.\n\n\n**Implementing New Features**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented reporting of clean verification results, preserving the original photo. I\'m also now building Digital Lockdown shortcuts for Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and Location settings. These shortcuts clearly disclose that they open official system panels. Furthermore, I am generating 6-digit retrieval codes for Burner Notes with a 24-hour expiry. I\'m storing them in a Supabase table, utilizing a single-use atomic function for retrieval and deletion. The notes\' function now handles rate limiting, validation and has timeout handling. Finally, I\'m documenting the SQL migration and function.\n\n\n**Testing Gesture Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on testing the gesture components. I\'ve started by building and validating the SecretGestureDetector, which handles the logo press and touch coordinate tracking. It correctly cancels gestures based on movement and time. I am now working on photo EXIF cleaning, verification tests, and the burner note code generation and validation tests. After completing these tests, I will integrate the end-to-end regression test suite.\n\n\n**Refining Sanitization & Shield**\n\nI\'m currently working on detailed aspects of the photo sanitizer. Specifically, I am refining the sanitization process by inspecting both the input and output images, with the `ExifInterface`. I\'m confirming that the output lacks GPS coordinates, altitude, camera details, and any user comments. Also, I\'m developing a testable helper for the delta cancellation logic within the shield functionality. I\'m focusing on ensuring it handles user touch coordinates correctly.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Components**\n\nI\'m now building the components for the secret dashboard. I\'ve integrated a POST request to Supabase for Burner Notes creation and an RPC call for atomic retrieval and deletion. I\'m focusing on rate limiting attempts client-side to prevent code brute-forcing. I\'ve also built a helper for constructing WhatsApp relay URIs. Finally, I\'m integrating the secret dashboard with tiles for photo sanitization, digital lockdown, and burner notes, along with a WhatsApp relay link for emergency contacts. I\'ve also implemented auto-closing when the app goes into the background, ensuring it is hidden.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_554184"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.core.security\\n\\nimport android.content.Context\\nimport android.os.Build\\nimport android.os.VibrationEffect\\nimport android.os.Vibrator\\nimport androidx.compose.foundation.gestures.awaitEachGesture\\nimport androidx.compose.foundation.gestures.awaitFirstDown\\nimport androidx.compose.ui.Modifier\\nimport androidx.compose.ui.geometry.Offset\\nimport androidx.compose.ui.input.pointer.PointerInputChange\\nimport androidx.compose.ui.input.pointer.pointerInput\\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.delay\\nimport kotlin.math.sqrt\\n\\nobject SecretGestureConfig {\\n  const val HOLD_DURATION_MS = 3000L\\n  const val MAX_MOVEMENT_DELTA_PX = 20.0f\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Evaluates if a pointer offset drift exceeds the 20-pixel cancellation threshold.\\n   * Public for deterministic unit testing.\\n   */\\n  fun isDriftExceeded(start: Offset, current: Offset, maxDeltaPx: Float = MAX_MOVEMENT_DELTA_PX): Boolean {\\n    val dx = current.x - start.x\\n    val dy = current.y - start.y\\n    val distance = sqrt((dx * dx + dy * dy).toDouble()).toFloat()\\n    return distance > maxDeltaPx\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Modifier that triggers a secret callback only when the user holds\\n * without moving more than 20 pixels for 3 full seconds.\\n * Triggers a short haptic vibration pulse on success.\\n */\\nfun Modifier.secretShieldHold(\\n  context: Context,\\n  isSosActive: Boolean,\\n  onActivated: () -> Unit\\n): Modifier = this.pointerInput(isSosActive) {\\n  if (isSosActive) return@pointerInput // Locked out while SOS is active\\n\\n  awaitEachGesture {\\n    val down: PointerInputChange = awaitFirstDown(requireUnconsumed = false)\\n    val startPos = down.position\\n    var isCancelled = false\\n    val startTime = System.currentTimeMillis()\\n\\n    while (!isCancelled) {\\n      val event = awaitPointerEvent()\\n      val currentPointer = event.changes.firstOrNull { it.id == down.id }\\n\\n      if (currentPointer == null || !currentPointer.pressed) {\\n        // Released before 3000ms\\n        isCancelled = true\\n        break\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check if finger moved more than 20 pixels\\n      if (SecretGestureConfig.isDriftExceeded(startPos, currentPointer.position)) {\\n        isCancelled = true\\n        break\\n      }\\n\\n      // Check if 3 seconds elapsed\\n      if (System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime >= SecretGestureConfig.HOLD_DURATION_MS) {\\n        // Haptic feedback confirmation\\n        triggerHapticPulse(context)\\n        onActivated()\\n        break\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nprivate fun triggerHapticPulse(context: Context) {\\n  try {\\n    val vibrator = context.getSystemService(Context.VIBRATOR_SERVICE) as? Vibrator\\n    if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.O) {\\n      vibrator?.vibrate(VibrationEffect.createOneShot(60, VibrationEffect.DEFAULT_AMPLITUDE))\\n    } else {\\n      @Suppress(\\\"DEPRECATION\\\")\\n      vibrator?.vibrate(60)\\n    }\\n  } catch (_: Exception) {}\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Implement SecretGestureDetector with 3s hold, 20px delta check, and haptic feedback\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/core/security/SecretGestureDetector.kt\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing SecretGestureDetector\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create SecretGestureDetector.kt\"}"
