    thinking: "**Constructing Burner Note Repository**\n\nI\'m currently building the `BurnerNoteRepository.kt` file. My focus is on generating a random 6-digit retrieval code for notes and implementing a 24-hour expiration. I need to persist these notes in the `burner_notes` Supabase table and ensure an atomic read-and-delete operation using a Supabase RPC function named `read_`. I\'m starting to think about how to best structure the data persistence and retrieval.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1019159"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.data.network\\n\\nimport android.content.Context\\nimport android.util.Log\\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.Dispatchers\\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.withContext\\nimport okhttp3.MediaType.Companion.toMediaType\\nimport okhttp3.OkHttpClient\\nimport okhttp3.Request\\nimport okhttp3.RequestBody.Companion.toRequestBody\\nimport org.json.JSONArray\\nimport org.json.JSONObject\\nimport java.security.SecureRandom\\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit\\n\\nsealed class BurnerNoteRetrieveResult {\\n  data class Success(val noteContent: String) : BurnerNoteRetrieveResult()\\n  data object AlreadyDestroyedOrExpired : BurnerNoteRetrieveResult()\\n  data object RateLimited : BurnerNoteRetrieveResult()\\n  data class Error(val message: String) : BurnerNoteRetrieveResult()\\n}\\n\\nclass BurnerNoteRepository(private val context: Context) {\\n\\n  companion object {\\n    private const val TAG = \\\"BurnerNoteRepo\\\"\\n    private const val MIN_REQUEST_INTERVAL_MS = 1500L\\n  }\\n\\n  private val client = OkHttpClient.Builder()\\n    .connectTimeout(15, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\\n    .readTimeout(15, TimeUnit.SECONDS)\\n    .build()\\n\\n  private val jsonMediaType = \\\"application/json; charset=utf-8\\\".toMediaType()\\n  private val secureRandom = SecureRandom()\\n  private var lastAttemptTimestamp = 0L\\n\\n  private fun getBaseUrl(): String = SupabaseConfig.getSupabaseUrl(context).trimEnd(\'/\')\\n  private fun getAnonKey(): String = SupabaseConfig.getSupabaseAnonKey(context)\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Generates a cryptographically strong 6-digit numerical retrieval code.\\n   */\\n  fun generateSixDigitCode(): String {\\n    val num = secureRandom.nextInt(900000) + 100000\\n    return num.toString()\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Stores a note with a 24-hour expiry in the burner_notes table.\\n   */\\n  suspend fun createBurnerNote(noteBody: String): Result<String> = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {\\n    if (noteBody.isBlank()) {\\n      return@withContext Result.failure(IllegalArgumentException(\\\"Note body cannot be empty.\\\"))\\n    }\\n\\n    val code = generateSixDigitCode()\\n    val url = \\\"${getBaseUrl()}/rest/v1/burner_notes\\\"\\n\\n    val payload = JSONObject().apply {\\n      put(\\\"access_code\\\", code)\\n      put(\\\"note_body\\\", noteBody)\\n    }\\n\\n    try {\\n      val request = Request.Builder()\\n        .url(url)\\n        .addHeader(\\\"apikey\\\", getAnonKey())\\n        .addHeader(\\\"Authorization\\\", \\\"Bearer ${getAnonKey()}\\\")\\n        .addHeader(\\\"Prefer\\\", \\\"return=minimal\\\")\\n        .post(payload.toString().toRequestBody(jsonMediaType))\\n        .build()\\n\\n      client.newCall(request).execute().use { response ->\\n        if (response.isSuccessful) {\\n          Result.success(code)\\n        } else {\\n          Result.failure(Exception(\\\"Failed to create note: HTTP ${response.code}\\\"))\\n        }\\n      }\\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\\n      Result.failure(e)\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * Atomically reads and deletes a note via the server-side RPC function read_and_burn.\\n   * Enforces client-side rate limiting to mitigate brute-force attempts.\\n   */\\n  suspend fun retrieveAndBurn(code: String): BurnerNoteRetrieveResult = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {\\n    val cleanCode = code.trim()\\n    if (cleanCode.length != 6 || !cleanCode.all { it.isDigit() }) {\\n      return@withContext BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.Error(\\\"Code must be exactly 6 numeric digits.\\\")\\n    }\\n\\n    val now = System.currentTimeMillis()\\n    if (now - lastAttemptTimestamp < MIN_REQUEST_INTERVAL_MS) {\\n      return@withContext BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.RateLimited\\n    }\\n    lastAttemptTimestamp = now\\n\\n    val url = \\\"${getBaseUrl()}/rest/v1/rpc/read_and_burn\\\"\\n    val payload = JSONObject().apply {\\n      put(\\\"p_code\\\", cleanCode)\\n    }\\n\\n    try {\\n      val request = Request.Builder()\\n        .url(url)\\n        .addHeader(\\\"apikey\\\", getAnonKey())\\n        .addHeader(\\\"Authorization\\\", \\\"Bearer ${getAnonKey()}\\\")\\n        .post(payload.toString().toRequestBody(jsonMediaType))\\n        .build()\\n\\n      client.newCall(request).execute().use { response ->\\n        if (!response.isSuccessful) {\\n          return@withContext BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.Error(\\\"HTTP ${response.code}: ${response.message}\\\")\\n        }\\n\\n        val bodyStr = response.body?.string() ?: \\\"\\\"\\n        parseRpcResponse(bodyStr)\\n      }\\n    } catch (e: Exception) {\\n      Log.w(TAG, \\\"Network failure retrieving note: ${e.message}\\\")\\n      BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.Error(\\\"Connection error: ${e.message}\\\")\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  private fun parseRpcResponse(bodyStr: String): BurnerNoteRetrieveResult {\\n    return try {\\n      val jsonArray = JSONArray(bodyStr)\\n      if (jsonArray.length() == 0) {\\n        return BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.AlreadyDestroyedOrExpired\\n      }\\n      val firstObj = jsonArray.getJSONObject(0)\\n      val isValid = firstObj.optBoolean(\\\"is_valid\\\", false)\\n      val content = firstObj.optString(\\\"note_content\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n\\n      if (isValid && content.isNotBlank()) {\\n        BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.Success(content)\\n      } else {\\n        BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.AlreadyDestroyedOrExpired\\n      }\\n    } catch (_: Exception) {\\n      // In case the RPC returns a single JSONObject instead of an array\\n      try {\\n        val jsonObj = JSONObject(bodyStr)\\n        val isValid = jsonObj.optBoolean(\\\"is_valid\\\", false)\\n        val content = jsonObj.optString(\\\"note_content\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n        if (isValid && content.isNotBlank()) {\\n          BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.Success(content)\\n        } else {\\n          BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.AlreadyDestroyedOrExpired\\n        }\\n      } catch (_: Exception) {\\n        BurnerNoteRetrieveResult.AlreadyDestroyedOrExpired\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Implement BurnerNoteRepository with 6-digit codes, atomic RPC read_and_burn, and rate limiting\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/network/BurnerNoteRepository.kt\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing BurnerNoteRepository\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create BurnerNoteRepository.kt\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\316\b\n\313\b\001i\024}\023:f&KP\332WI\365\336\325\262\217|\241Zg\375\245\257_E\234\f\3619\365)\020\034\222S\202\026\v\b\212\215\311\005\366\323\t\223\240S*\275\035Jj\201\320\320\n\v\217m\342\211\222\376M\001[\234-\3101\257\017\352\251\266\314S\244\300\030|\271[C\237l\026\304\212)?\034\306\273i\360\003\223\025%\354\231\210\376\240\022|y\233\360\003\300\024\345\005\372\326\\\352\023\323\276e\357\3450o4\365o\347\264\262\360\373\274/}v\200\303u}\225\274\336FO\231}\314\226O\311\304\205\341\241\b/\336;\337\302\335\302\\\373JgQ]E\025=\240g\263R\341>X\275S\251\320R\201\227}\320\376\323u\023V\376\215H\355\340V\344\331\366\240\332Q\327\274QDl\244D\0216\242\336\323\002X\210\224|\003^\213\344\33530X-\327Z\346\305\025\320\237M!\317\316\303r\026Y\005}B8\267\025JU\255\004\201*\234k\272-\000\257\235\017\377)\321\276\342/\n\302\323\366\036\275\247\202\000\240y\266\306\236z\260\246\273\364\356\340?\035\230\362\020\223\'\2252?tY\272<\254\315bB\373}\210\255\246y\212\r\357]\362\262\2664\373\016\252G\254A\344\341\344\221a>\350\033\234\364\017\031\213\215\207\354\266\224\320y\316\356\306X\022\234\nF\037\302\016\362\244\270\035\355\2734\2021#\b\257\230\362\342uc\037j\270\353Q\362\221\341\253\304\033M<\234;\327\310:\242\032\362\"\f\200\f<\304f\331\222\313\206-~\211\n\376(\316\036\3362\214\373\262\'\223\"\263\213\333F\3253m3\001J\br\263\035\245W0\0378\362>#\000\201\332\304J\226\327\2746\0318\223\323T\325H%\022\376\351\243\032\334\300\320\231\345\232\216iS\372\b\223y\340\217\206-\240j\354\344F\016\361\275\306\322_-\236\0370K\356\027\227u\212!<VkX\330\"\376)L/kM\254S\343\021|\355\244\217^\020R\320i\\\205\355\211\322!\222#S\256\353N\316\253\267\031\230\261\320\314A\376\224K\271\f\20485\266u`\342\240\276`\351c\306z\vso\'V\005\236L\025\323\362\234f\200G\262<\022\017\267\274m\356cV\251\224\270\357\304a9t\320\v/\251\362\017\t\314\"\211\247\017\277`}\2571\002\223#Q\300\nCh\356l\221\242r\357%\t\033\035\340\033&*\247YR\345?\037\b\304\357\202\035\360S\360\371Z\3014\300<