    user_response: "## BUG FIX: DURESS PIN OPENS PETAL BUT SOS STATUS IS UNCLEAR\n\nIn my current Cloak Android app, entering the duress PIN opens the period-tracker screen, just like the normal PIN.\n\nThe visible tracker screen is intentional. However, according to my architecture, entering the duress PIN must also silently activate the SOS workflow.\n\nPlease inspect the existing code and fix this behavior without changing the intended disguise.\n\n### Required behavior\n\n1. Entering the normal PIN opens the Petal period tracker without activating SOS.\n2. Entering the duress PIN opens the exact same Petal period tracker while activating the SOS controller.\n3. SOS activation must not depend on which screen is visible.\n4. Ensure the SOS controller starts only once per activation.\n5. Verify that the active SOS state persists when navigating between screens or entering Fake-Sleep.\n6. Verify that the SOS workflow attempts the configured emergency actions, including location acquisition, SMS to configured contacts, and audio recording when the necessary permissions and Android execution conditions permit.\n7. Do not claim SMS delivery, location sharing, or audio upload succeeded unless it is verified.\n8. Do not expose an obvious SOS banner, alert, or emergency screen on the disguised tracker.\n9. Add automated tests proving that the normal PIN does not activate SOS and the duress PIN does activate SOS while both return to the same tracker screen.\n\n### Diagnose before modifying\n\nIdentify the PIN verification function, the normal-versus-duress PIN decision, and the SOS controller entry point. Trace the duress PIN execution path and explain why SOS is not visibly or functionally confirmed.\n\nMake the smallest safe changes necessary. Do not rebuild the app or replace existing working architecture.\n\nAfter fixing, run the relevant tests and report:\n- Whether normal PIN activates SOS: PASS/FAIL.\n- Whether duress PIN activates SOS: PASS/FAIL.\n- Whether both PINs open the same tracker: PASS/FAIL.\n- Whether the SOS controller is genuinely invoked: PASS/FAIL.\n- Which real device features cannot be verified in the AI Studio preview.\n\nDo not mark the fix complete merely because the tracker screen appears."
    items {
      text: "## BUG FIX: DURESS PIN OPENS PETAL BUT SOS STATUS IS UNCLEAR\n\nIn my current Cloak Android app, entering the duress PIN opens the period-tracker screen, just like the normal PIN.\n\nThe visible tracker screen is intentional. However, according to my architecture, entering the duress PIN must also silently activate the SOS workflow.\n\nPlease inspect the existing code and fix this behavior without changing the intended disguise.\n\n### Required behavior\n\n1. Entering the normal PIN opens the Petal period tracker without activating SOS.\n2. Entering the duress PIN opens the exact same Petal period tracker while activating the SOS controller.\n3. SOS activation must not depend on which screen is visible.\n4. Ensure the SOS controller starts only once per activation.\n5. Verify that the active SOS state persists when navigating between screens or entering Fake-Sleep.\n6. Verify that the SOS workflow attempts the configured emergency actions, including location acquisition, SMS to configured contacts, and audio recording when the necessary permissions and Android execution conditions permit.\n7. Do not claim SMS delivery, location sharing, or audio upload succeeded unless it is verified.\n8. Do not expose an obvious SOS banner, alert, or emergency screen on the disguised tracker.\n9. Add automated tests proving that the normal PIN does not activate SOS and the duress PIN does activate SOS while both return to the same tracker screen.\n\n### Diagnose before modifying\n\nIdentify the PIN verification function, the normal-versus-duress PIN decision, and the SOS controller entry point. Trace the duress PIN execution path and explain why SOS is not visibly or functionally confirmed.\n\nMake the smallest safe changes necessary. Do not rebuild the app or replace existing working architecture.\n\nAfter fixing, run the relevant tests and report:\n- Whether normal PIN activates SOS: PASS/FAIL.\n- Whether duress PIN activates SOS: PASS/FAIL.\n- Whether both PINs open the same tracker: PASS/FAIL.\n- Whether the SOS controller is genuinely invoked: PASS/FAIL.\n- Which real device features cannot be verified in the AI Studio preview.\n\nDo not mark the fix complete merely because the tracker screen appears."
    }
  }
}
