  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Tracing the Implementation**\n\nI\'ve been tracing the implementation within `TrackerMainScreen.kt`, focusing specifically on the `isSosActive` variable. Initially, I found it was derived directly from the `sosState`, but now the code uses the `sosController.isSosActive` property. I\'m trying to understand the rationale behind this change, so I\'m investigating the behavior and implications.\n\n\n**Analyzing SOS Activation**\n\nI\'ve realized that not using `collectAsState()` means triggering `sosController.startSos()` won\'t recompose `isSosActive` in `TrackerMainScreen`. I\'m now looking at SOS confirmation and the duress PIN implementation. The goal is to ensure the SOS controller activates when the duress PIN is entered, without changing the visible screen or activating SOS unnecessarily. I\'m focusing on ensuring the SOS state persists across navigation.\n\n\n**Verifying Emergency Actions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on verifying the SOS workflow. I\'m ensuring that configured emergency actions, like location acquisition, SMS sending to contacts, and audio recording, are attempted when permissions and Android execution conditions are met. I\'m also ensuring delivery, location sharing, and audio upload verification before claiming success. The disguised tracker\'s SOS activation also needs to remain discreet, and automated tests are being implemented to differentiate between normal and duress PINs. I\'m adding a diagnostic card to Settings to help with testing and verification.\n\n\n"
