  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Service Start**\n\nI\'ve been examining `SosController.kt`, specifically focusing on the launch of the foreground service. I\'m noting the try-catch block around `SosForegroundService.startService()`. The intention is clearly to initiate the service for continuous audio chunking and notifications. I\'m paying close attention to the exception handling, as failures here could be critical to the application\'s functionality.\n\n\n**Reviewing Keypad Verification**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to `KeypadScreen.kt` within the context of duress and normal PIN verification. I see the `LaunchedEffect` is verifying entered pins. I\'m focusing on the `when` block to understand how SOS is triggered or stopped based on pin type. This is key to understanding the duress feature, and I\'m analyzing the `sosController.startSos()` call with the \"duress\\_pin\" trigger. I\'m also cross-referencing this with the `FakeSleepOverlay.kt` implementation.\n\n\n**Clarifying Unlock Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the unlock flow in `KeypadScreen.kt`. It looks like if the normal PIN unlocks the device, `sosController.stopSos()` is triggered, alongside `onUnlockSuccess()`. I see that the same `onUnlockSuccess()` is also triggered on a successful duress PIN entry, but the key difference is that `sosController.startSos()` is called first with \"duress_pin\". It appears the duress PIN should keep SOS active. I need to fully grasp why the user reported an issue about the duress PIN functionality!\n\n\n**Fixing Stealth Activation**\n\nI\'m now investigating the stealth activation requirement. My goal is to fix the duress PIN behavior. I\'m focusing on ensuring SOS initiates only once with the duress PIN, regardless of screen visibility. I\'m also ensuring the service persists across navigation and Fake-Sleep, and attempting emergency actions as configured and permissions permit. Critically, I\'m ensuring no premature claims about successful actions are made.\n\n\n**Tracing Duress Execution**\n\nI\'m now tracing the duress PIN execution flow. I see `PinStorage.kt` handles PIN verification, calling into the `CryptoManager` for encryption. `KeypadScreen.kt` clearly distinguishes between normal and duress PIN verification results. My immediate focus is now on confirming that duress PIN verification invokes `sosController.startSos()`, with the intention being to remain in SOS mode. I\'m verifying the SOS controller entry point is correctly invoked.\n\n\n**Diagnosing State Reactivity**\n\nI\'ve discovered critical state reactivity issues within the `TrackerMainScreen.kt` and `FakeSleepOverlay.kt` related to SOS activation. The `isSosActive` property, when not collected reactively, failed to reflect the asynchronous state transitions after the duress PIN entry. I\'m focusing on the fix using `collectAsState()` for proper reactivity, ensuring that the screen updates correctly, and also ensuring the Fake-Sleep overlay responds to the duress SOS activation. I\'m making sure that SOS start state is also visibly displayed. I also see that there is no status indicator or diagnostics reporting for the user\'s status within settings and am working on designing a stealth-friendly solution.\n\n\n**Implementing Status Diagnostics**\n\nI\'m now implementing diagnostics within the `SettingsTabView` in `TrackerMainScreen.kt`. I\'m focusing on providing discreet \"Guardian Engine Status\" indicators. I\'m adding status reports in the settings, including Guardian Status (Active/Idle), Session ID, and Trigger Source. I\'m also ensuring the settings displays current status of location/SMS/audio actions that have been dispatched. I\'m focusing on ensuring these diagnostics are stealth-friendly.\n\n\n**Adding Status Reporting**\n\nI\'m now incorporating the new \"Guardian Engine Status\" into `SettingsTabView` within `TrackerMainScreen.kt`. I\'m integrating the provided diagnostics, including trigger timestamp, session ID, and status of various emergency actions (SMS, GPS, audio) within settings. Crucially, I\'m ensuring that a discreet \"Stop Guardian Session\" button is implemented to allow controlled testing and deactivation from settings. I\'m focusing on a clean integration.\n\n\n"
