  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Protection Status**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a \"Guardian Protection Status\" card within the `SettingsTabView`, positioned directly beneath the \"Security Reset\" option. I\'ve begun to consider the logic for display: If `sosState` is `SosState.Active`, the card should show \"Protection Status: Active\" (triggered by `current.triggerSource`), and should display the status message `current.statusMessage`.\n\n\n**Refining Active State Display**\n\nI\'m now detailing the active protection status. It will show the latest location (`current.lastMapsUrl`), indicate emergency SMS dispatch to support contacts, and confirm ongoing audio evidence capture. The action button will be \"Stop Guardian Protection,\" calling `sosController.stopSos()`. When idle, I\'ll show \"Armed & Standing by,\" with ready SMS/location features. I\'m double-checking `SosController.kt` to verify that `startSos(\"duress_pin\")` behaves as expected.\n\n\n**Verifying Component Integration**\n\nI\'m now confirming the integration of the SOS state and controller within `SettingsTabView`. I\'ve verified the pass-through of `sosState` and `sosController` from `TrackerMainScreen.kt` at lines 120-135 and 220-240, and confirmed the declaration of `SettingsTabView`. I\'m checking that the necessary data is correctly passed so that I can display the protection status card accurately.\n\n\n**Confirming Status Rendering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the `SettingsTabView` will render the Guardian Protection status. I\'m building out the `Guardian Protection Status Card`. The color of the card changes if `sosState` is `SosState.Active`. I\'m using a `Card` composable, with a `Column` to hold contents. The card will react to the current SOS state.\n\n\n**Designing Visual Feedback**\n\nI\'m now detailing visual indicators for the \"Guardian Protection\" card within `SettingsTabView`. I\'m using an icon that changes based on the `sosState` (active or inactive) and a box around the content with different background colors and padding. I\'ve designed the visual styling for the card, to improve the user\'s perception of active and inactive protection.\n\n\n\n**Refining Card Text**\n\nI\'m now detailing the text for the Guardian Protection status. I\'m incorporating an \"ACTIVE\" or \"ARMED\" label with appropriate color and styling. I\'m also including detailed descriptions of what the Guardian is doing in each state (idle or active), including information about SMS alerts and audio capture. I am making sure to correctly identify the trigger source.\n\n\n"
