  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Keypad Screen Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the logic within `AppNavHost.kt`, specifically focusing on `KeypadScreen`. I\'ve found that a successful normal PIN entry triggers `sosController.stopSos()` and subsequently navigates to `Screen.Tracker` via `onUnlockSuccess()`. Conversely, entering a duress PIN initiates `sosController.startSos(\"duress\")`.\n\n\n**Testing SOS Activation Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into requirement 9 and creating a test file, `DuressPinAndSosActivationTest.kt`, to ensure the correct SOS behavior. I\'m focusing on validating that the normal PIN *doesn\'t* activate SOS, and the duress PIN *does*, even though they both navigate to the same tracker screen. I will write a test that checks the state of `sosController.isSosActive`.\n\n\n"
