  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Settings Tab**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `SettingsTabView` with these parameters: `contactRepository`, `periodRepository`, `pinStorage`, `sosState`, and `sosController`. These are fundamental to my design, representing core functionalities for contacts, periods, security, and SOS features, respectively. I\'m focusing on ensuring these parameters are correctly injected and utilized within the `SettingsTabView` composable.\n\n\n**Integrating Guardian Status**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the Guardian Protection Status card into the settings view, placing it directly after the \"Security Reset\" section. I\'m dynamically updating the card\'s color and icon based on the SOS state, providing visual feedback to the user. I also added discreet verification in settings as a safety measure. The layout uses a `Card` composable for the visual structure, and a `Column` with `Row` for organizing the content.\n\n\n**Visualizing Guardian Status**\n\nI am now focusing on the visual representation of the guardian status within the settings view. The UI elements, like the security icon\'s color and the text label, are being dynamically updated based on the `sosState`. I\'m using `Box` composables for the status indicators. These visually distinguish active and armed states with color-coded backgrounds and text labels.\n\n\n**Describing Guardian Status**\n\nNow I\'m creating descriptions for the various SOS states. I\'ve defined descriptions for idle and active states, using typography styles for clarity. The active state includes the trigger source and a status message. I\'m leveraging material theming for consistent styling.\n\n\n**Displaying SOS Information**\n\nI\'m now integrating live location URLs into the settings view, displaying them as clickable links when available. I\'ve included the update count and cadence information to provide context. The style uses a medium font weight for the live location and a small label for the update details. Finally, there\'s a prominent button to stop the active SOS session.\n\n\n"
