            lines {
              text: "  val tips = listOf("
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"1. Hydration & Prostaglandins\" to \"Drinking 2.5L of warm water daily helps flush excess sodium and decreases uterine prostaglandin cramping.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"2. Magnesium for Cramp Relief\" to \"Magnesium glycinate (300mg) relaxes uterine smooth muscles and diminishes period pain naturally.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"3. Iron Replenishment during Flow\" to \"Consume dark leafy greens, lentils, and lean proteins with vitamin C to maximize dietary non-heme iron absorption.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"4. Sleep Architecture in Luteal Phase\" to \"Elevated progesterone can raise resting body temperature by 0.5\302\260C; keep your bedroom at 18\302\260C for optimal deep REM sleep.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"5. Cycle-Synched Fitness\" to \"Engage in strength and HIIT workouts during follicular phase when estrogen peaks; switch to gentle yoga during menstruation.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"6. Fiber for Estrogen Balance\" to \"Cruciferous vegetables (broccoli, cabbage) provide indole-3-carbinol which supports the liver in metabolizing circulating estrogen.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"7. Heat Therapy vs Pain Mediators\" to \"Applying a heating pad (40\302\260C) over the lower pelvic area increases local microvascular blood flow as effectively as ibuprofen.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"8. Caffeine\'s Effect on Breast Tissue\" to \"Reducing coffee during the week prior to menstruation significantly decreases cyclic mastalgia (breast tenderness).\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"9. Vitamin B6 & Neurotransmitters\" to \"Pyridoxine (Vitamin B6) acts as an essential cofactor in dopamine and serotonin synthesis, counteracting premenstrual dysphoria.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"10. Follicular Phase Energy Ascent\" to \"Rising estradiol levels enhance insulin sensitivity and mitochondrial ATP generation, resulting in increased clarity.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"11. Ovulation Identification\" to \"Clear, stretchy \'egg-white\' cervical mucus and a slight basal body temperature spike signal your 24-hour fertile window.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"12. Anti-Inflammatory Nutrition\" to \"Omega-3 fatty acids from walnuts, flaxseed, and salmon compete with arachidonic acid to reduce inflammatory thromboxanes.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"13. Chamomile & Ginger Teas\" to \"Gingerol in steeped ginger tea suppresses COX-2 enzyme activity, relieving nausea and menstrual bloating.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    \"14. Consistent Hormonal Tracking\" to \"Recording your cycle over 3+ months enables accurate variance tracking between anovulatory and ovulatory cycles.\","
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
