  planner_response {
    response: "# DURESS PIN & SOS ACTIVATION FIX REPORT\n\n## 1. Technical Diagnosis & Root-Cause Analysis\n\n### Code Inspection & Architecture Trace\n1. **PIN Verification Function**:\n   - `PinStorage.verify(pin)` in `com.example.core.security.PinStorage`.\n   - Normal PIN derivation: `CryptoManager.verifyPin(pin, normalSalt, normalHash)`.\n   - Duress PIN derivation: `CryptoManager.verifyPin(pin, duressSalt, duressHash)`.\n   - Returned `PinVerificationResult.NormalPinSuccess` or `PinVerificationResult.DuressPinSuccess`.\n\n2. **Normal-versus-Duress Decision Point**:\n   - In `KeypadScreen.kt`:\n     ```kotlin\n     when (result) {\n       is PinVerificationResult.NormalPinSuccess -> {\n         if (sosController.isSosActive) { sosController.stopSos() }\n         onUnlockSuccess()\n       }\n       is PinVerificationResult.DuressPinSuccess -> {\n         sosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")\n         onUnlockSuccess()\n       }\n       ...\n     }\n     ```\n     Both paths correctly navigated to `onUnlockSuccess()`, opening `Screen.Tracker.route` (the Petal period tracker disguise).\n\n3. **SOS Controller Entry Point**:\n   - `SosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")`.\n\n4. **Why SOS Status Was Functionally Unclear & Non-Reactive**:\n   - **Root Cause A (State Reactivity Gap)**: In `TrackerMainScreen.kt`, line 124 read `val isSosActive = sosController.isSosActive`. This was a raw property read on an ordinary Kotlin getter (`_state.value is SosState.Active`), **not a collected Compose state**. When `startSos()` was launched asynchronously during navigation, Compose had no subscription to `sosController.state` (`StateFlow<SosState>`), preventing recomposition. Consequently, `FakeSleepOverlay(isSosActive = ...)` and downstream components never observed the active state.\n   - **Root Cause B (Absence of Discreet In-App Verification)**: While the architecture strictly forbids showing any conspicuous emergency banners, alerts, or dialogs on the public period calendar disguise (Requirement 8), the Settings tab had no diagnostic indicator showing whether the background safety engine was `Idle` or `Active`. Testers and users inspecting Settings had no way to confirm that the duress PIN had engaged the background SOS session.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Minimal Safe Changes Applied\n\n1. **Reactive State Collection in `TrackerMainScreen.kt`**:\n   - Replaced static getter with reactive Flow collection:\n     ```kotlin\n     val sosState by sosController.state.collectAsState()\n     val isSosActive = sosState is SosState.Active\n     ```\n   - Connected `sosState` to `FakeSleepOverlay` so that the 15-second inactivity timer reliably triggers during active SOS sessions.\n\n2. **Discreet Guardian Protection Verification Card in Settings**:\n   - Added a low-profile **Guardian Protection** status card inside `SettingsTabView` (Settings tab):\n     - When Idle: Displays `\"ARMED\"` with confirmation that background detection is ready.\n     - When Active: Displays `\"ACTIVE\"` with trigger source (`\"duress_pin\"` or `\"shake\"`), live status message, latest Maps link (`https://maps.google.com/?q=...`), update sequence count, and an explicit `\"Stop Active SOS Session\"` button.\n   - Preserved complete stealth on the public home screen (Calendar, Log, and Tips tabs show zero emergency UI).\n\n3. **Lifecycle & Navigation Persistence**:\n   - Verified that `SosController` is held as an application-level singleton in `CloakApplication`. Screen navigation (e.g., locking the app or entering Fake-Sleep) does not interrupt or reset the active SOS session.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Automated Test Verification Results\n\nA dedicated automated test suite (`DuressPinAndSosActivationTest.kt`) was written and executed alongside all regression tests:\n\n```\nTask :app:compileDebugKotlin UP-TO-DATE\nTask :app:compileDebugUnitTestKotlin UP-TO-DATE\nTask :app:testDebugUnitTest\n\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > normalPin_unlocksToTrackerWithoutActivatingSos PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > duressPin_activatesSosAndOpensSameTrackerScreen PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > duressPin_repeatedEntryMaintainsExistingSessionIdempotently PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > normalPin_stopsActiveSosSessionAndReturnsToTracker PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > activeSos_persistsAcrossFakeSleepAndScreenNavigation PASSED\n\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > cryptoManager_hashesPinWithRandomSaltAndVerifiesCorrectly PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_rejectsInvalidLengthOrIdenticalPins PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_distinguishesNormalAndDuressCredentials PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_identifiesThreeSpikesWithProperSpacing PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_ignoresNormalWalkingMovementBelowThreshold PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > sosController_idempotentDuressTriggerAndNormalStop PASSED\n\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > periodRepository_persistsEntriesAndPredictsCycleAccurately PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > contactRepository_enforcesMaximumThreeContacts PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > locationProvider_formatsGoogleMapsUrlWithoutApiKeyRequirement PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > smsDispatcher_handlesNoContactsGracefully PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > supabaseSosRepository_rejectsEmptyOrNonExistentAudioFiles PASSED\n\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > secretGesture_cancelsWhenMovementExceedsTwentyPixels PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > burnerNoteRepository_generatesCryptographicSixDigitCodes PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > burnerNoteRepository_validatesCodeFormatAndRejectsShortCodes PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > photoSanitizer_cleansImageAndVerifiesAbsenceOfMetadata PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > digitalLockdown_safelyExecutesSettingShortcuts PASSED\n\nExampleUnitTest > addition_isCorrect PASSED\nExampleRobolectricTest > read string from context PASSED\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 30s\n33 actionable tasks: 5 executed, 28 up-to-date\n```\n\n**Total Tests: 23 PASSED, 0 FAILED.**\n\n---\n\n## 4. Required Behavior Verification Report\n\n| Requirement | Result | Evidence / Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1. Normal PIN does not activate SOS** | **PASS** | Verified in `normalPin_unlocksToTrackerWithoutActivatingSos`. `sosController.isSosActive` remains `false` (`SosState.Idle`). |\n| **2. Duress PIN activates SOS** | **PASS** | Verified in `duressPin_activatesSosAndOpensSameTrackerScreen`. `sosController.isSosActive` transitions to `true` (`triggerSource = \"duress_pin\"`). |\n| **3. Both PINs open the same tracker** | **PASS** | Verified: both PIN paths navigate exclusively to `Screen.Tracker.route` (`TrackerMainScreen`). |\n| **4. SOS controller is genuinely invoked** | **PASS** | Verified: `SosController.startSos(\"duress_pin\")` starts session UUID, triggers initial location fetch, dispatches SMS, and launches `SosForegroundService`. |\n| **5. Idempotent single activation** | **PASS** | Verified in `duressPin_repeatedEntryMaintainsExistingSessionIdempotently`: re-entering duress PIN preserves the existing active session without duplicate sends. |\n| **6. Active state persists across screens & Fake-Sleep** | **PASS** | Verified in `activeSos_persistsAcrossFakeSleepAndScreenNavigation`. |\n| **7. No visible SOS banner on disguise** | **PASS** | Calendar, Log, and Tips tabs display only menstrual wellness UI. Diagnostic status is tucked inside Settings > Guardian Protection. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Environment Constraints & Real-Device Features Disclosure\n\nThe following platform features were verified via automated unit/Robolectric test suites and local JVM services, but require a physical device for live hardware validation:\n\n1. **Cellular SMS Dispatch**: Real carrier SMS transmission requires a physical Android handset with an active SIM card and network signal. In the emulator/test environment, `SmsDispatcher` safely catches absent telephony SIMs without crashing.\n2. **Physical Accelerometer Shake**: Tested mathematically with synthetic linear acceleration samples ($18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $250\\,\\text{ms}$ spacing); physical device shake requires handheld device movement.\n3. **Hardware GPS Fix**: In the container environment, `LocationProvider` falls back gracefully when satellite locks are unavailable.\n4. **Android 14+ System Privacy Indicator**: The green microphone privacy dot displayed by the Android OS status bar during `SosForegroundService` execution requires an Android 14+ physical device to observe."
    modified_response: "# DURESS PIN & SOS ACTIVATION FIX REPORT\n\n## 1. Technical Diagnosis & Root-Cause Analysis\n\n### Code Inspection & Architecture Trace\n1. **PIN Verification Function**:\n   - `PinStorage.verify(pin)` in `com.example.core.security.PinStorage`.\n   - Normal PIN derivation: `CryptoManager.verifyPin(pin, normalSalt, normalHash)`.\n   - Duress PIN derivation: `CryptoManager.verifyPin(pin, duressSalt, duressHash)`.\n   - Returned `PinVerificationResult.NormalPinSuccess` or `PinVerificationResult.DuressPinSuccess`.\n\n2. **Normal-versus-Duress Decision Point**:\n   - In `KeypadScreen.kt`:\n     ```kotlin\n     when (result) {\n       is PinVerificationResult.NormalPinSuccess -> {\n         if (sosController.isSosActive) { sosController.stopSos() }\n         onUnlockSuccess()\n       }\n       is PinVerificationResult.DuressPinSuccess -> {\n         sosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")\n         onUnlockSuccess()\n       }\n       ...\n     }\n     ```\n     Both paths correctly navigated to `onUnlockSuccess()`, opening `Screen.Tracker.route` (the Petal period tracker disguise).\n\n3. **SOS Controller Entry Point**:\n   - `SosController.startSos(triggerSource = \"duress_pin\")`.\n\n4. **Why SOS Status Was Functionally Unclear & Non-Reactive**:\n   - **Root Cause A (State Reactivity Gap)**: In `TrackerMainScreen.kt`, line 124 read `val isSosActive = sosController.isSosActive`. This was a raw property read on an ordinary Kotlin getter (`_state.value is SosState.Active`), **not a collected Compose state**. When `startSos()` was launched asynchronously during navigation, Compose had no subscription to `sosController.state` (`StateFlow<SosState>`), preventing recomposition. Consequently, `FakeSleepOverlay(isSosActive = ...)` and downstream components never observed the active state.\n   - **Root Cause B (Absence of Discreet In-App Verification)**: While the architecture strictly forbids showing any conspicuous emergency banners, alerts, or dialogs on the public period calendar disguise (Requirement 8), the Settings tab had no diagnostic indicator showing whether the background safety engine was `Idle` or `Active`. Testers and users inspecting Settings had no way to confirm that the duress PIN had engaged the background SOS session.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Minimal Safe Changes Applied\n\n1. **Reactive State Collection in `TrackerMainScreen.kt`**:\n   - Replaced static getter with reactive Flow collection:\n     ```kotlin\n     val sosState by sosController.state.collectAsState()\n     val isSosActive = sosState is SosState.Active\n     ```\n   - Connected `sosState` to `FakeSleepOverlay` so that the 15-second inactivity timer reliably triggers during active SOS sessions.\n\n2. **Discreet Guardian Protection Verification Card in Settings**:\n   - Added a low-profile **Guardian Protection** status card inside `SettingsTabView` (Settings tab):\n     - When Idle: Displays `\"ARMED\"` with confirmation that background detection is ready.\n     - When Active: Displays `\"ACTIVE\"` with trigger source (`\"duress_pin\"` or `\"shake\"`), live status message, latest Maps link (`https://maps.google.com/?q=...`), update sequence count, and an explicit `\"Stop Active SOS Session\"` button.\n   - Preserved complete stealth on the public home screen (Calendar, Log, and Tips tabs show zero emergency UI).\n\n3. **Lifecycle & Navigation Persistence**:\n   - Verified that `SosController` is held as an application-level singleton in `CloakApplication`. Screen navigation (e.g., locking the app or entering Fake-Sleep) does not interrupt or reset the active SOS session.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Automated Test Verification Results\n\nA dedicated automated test suite (`DuressPinAndSosActivationTest.kt`) was written and executed alongside all regression tests:\n\n```\nTask :app:compileDebugKotlin UP-TO-DATE\nTask :app:compileDebugUnitTestKotlin UP-TO-DATE\nTask :app:testDebugUnitTest\n\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > normalPin_unlocksToTrackerWithoutActivatingSos PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > duressPin_activatesSosAndOpensSameTrackerScreen PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > duressPin_repeatedEntryMaintainsExistingSessionIdempotently PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > normalPin_stopsActiveSosSessionAndReturnsToTracker PASSED\nDuressPinAndSosActivationTest > activeSos_persistsAcrossFakeSleepAndScreenNavigation PASSED\n\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > cryptoManager_hashesPinWithRandomSaltAndVerifiesCorrectly PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_rejectsInvalidLengthOrIdenticalPins PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > pinStorage_distinguishesNormalAndDuressCredentials PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_identifiesThreeSpikesWithProperSpacing PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > shakeDetector_ignoresNormalWalkingMovementBelowThreshold PASSED\nStage1SafetyEngineTest > sosController_idempotentDuressTriggerAndNormalStop PASSED\n\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > periodRepository_persistsEntriesAndPredictsCycleAccurately PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > contactRepository_enforcesMaximumThreeContacts PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > locationProvider_formatsGoogleMapsUrlWithoutApiKeyRequirement PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > smsDispatcher_handlesNoContactsGracefully PASSED\nStage2DisguiseAndGuardianTest > supabaseSosRepository_rejectsEmptyOrNonExistentAudioFiles PASSED\n\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > secretGesture_cancelsWhenMovementExceedsTwentyPixels PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > burnerNoteRepository_generatesCryptographicSixDigitCodes PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > burnerNoteRepository_validatesCodeFormatAndRejectsShortCodes PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > photoSanitizer_cleansImageAndVerifiesAbsenceOfMetadata PASSED\nStage3DigitalShieldAndHardeningTest > digitalLockdown_safelyExecutesSettingShortcuts PASSED\n\nExampleUnitTest > addition_isCorrect PASSED\nExampleRobolectricTest > read string from context PASSED\n\nBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 30s\n33 actionable tasks: 5 executed, 28 up-to-date\n```\n\n**Total Tests: 23 PASSED, 0 FAILED.**\n\n---\n\n## 4. Required Behavior Verification Report\n\n| Requirement | Result | Evidence / Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1. Normal PIN does not activate SOS** | **PASS** | Verified in `normalPin_unlocksToTrackerWithoutActivatingSos`. `sosController.isSosActive` remains `false` (`SosState.Idle`). |\n| **2. Duress PIN activates SOS** | **PASS** | Verified in `duressPin_activatesSosAndOpensSameTrackerScreen`. `sosController.isSosActive` transitions to `true` (`triggerSource = \"duress_pin\"`). |\n| **3. Both PINs open the same tracker** | **PASS** | Verified: both PIN paths navigate exclusively to `Screen.Tracker.route` (`TrackerMainScreen`). |\n| **4. SOS controller is genuinely invoked** | **PASS** | Verified: `SosController.startSos(\"duress_pin\")` starts session UUID, triggers initial location fetch, dispatches SMS, and launches `SosForegroundService`. |\n| **5. Idempotent single activation** | **PASS** | Verified in `duressPin_repeatedEntryMaintainsExistingSessionIdempotently`: re-entering duress PIN preserves the existing active session without duplicate sends. |\n| **6. Active state persists across screens & Fake-Sleep** | **PASS** | Verified in `activeSos_persistsAcrossFakeSleepAndScreenNavigation`. |\n| **7. No visible SOS banner on disguise** | **PASS** | Calendar, Log, and Tips tabs display only menstrual wellness UI. Diagnostic status is tucked inside Settings > Guardian Protection. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Environment Constraints & Real-Device Features Disclosure\n\nThe following platform features were verified via automated unit/Robolectric test suites and local JVM services, but require a physical device for live hardware validation:\n\n1. **Cellular SMS Dispatch**: Real carrier SMS transmission requires a physical Android handset with an active SIM card and network signal. In the emulator/test environment, `SmsDispatcher` safely catches absent telephony SIMs without crashing.\n2. **Physical Accelerometer Shake**: Tested mathematically with synthetic linear acceleration samples ($18\\,\\text{m/s}^2$, $250\\,\\text{ms}$ spacing); physical device shake requires handheld device movement.\n3. **Hardware GPS Fix**: In the container environment, `LocationProvider` falls back gracefully when satellite locks are unavailable.\n4. **Android 14+ System Privacy Indicator**: The green microphone privacy dot displayed by the Android OS status bar during `SosForegroundService` execution requires an Android 14+ physical device to observe."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\232\002\n\227\002\001i\024}\023\351e\036\177\225d\207\2517\262\252\2448\006Ab\253^\241\'\321\031\021\310\335H\v\325\221\2347`\327\374k1\263\026\212\362Y\201%\216p\246\373qT\347o\350\357\213\2303G~n~\337\242\0330\3735\214\264\300@\363\254X\365\031Q\324\027\006\275\221\037i\343\207)a\a#\251\030?\210\323\2172\335,\230\254\277A4t]r\260\321\000\226C\017>\211\322\300\305\305\317J#\300\224\022\340\354S\315\277\343}f\017K\027\345\226\204a\214%dd\tt\002\216\246\215x\224 \245\032\253-\365b\027\252\026}#0\226Nk\000\315\350y\224\271\210\004Q\037\360\362\316\r\355)\252fjw\301\037\r\266\252)\265|\363\2312\030\225h\355\nR5\236\311\366\235*e\225,\330\340\306\317\3659=\320C\341\346\2134\023o\360\270\203R\201\200\371\200S\215\361\266\246\346\355\246;\240\347(\002\003\342\336\214H\271\371\322b\252\342\211\244]\307b\3472\0259\016ZG.\300"
