  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Test Coverage**\n\nI\'m currently focused on expanding the test suite, specifically targeting `AuthViewModel` integration within `DuressPinAndSosActivationTest.kt`. The initial step involves updating `KeypadScreen.kt` to appropriately delegate to or utilize `AuthViewModel` to guarantee state separation and lifecycle persistence.\n\n\n**Analyzing Screen Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into `Screen.kt`, specifically focusing on how the composable interacts with `AuthViewModel`. My goal is to streamline the delegation process, ensuring the view model handles state management and business logic effectively. I\'m keen on exploring how we can enhance testability by minimizing direct dependencies on the composable from the viewmodel. I\'m carefully considering how to make the composable observe ViewModel state changes.\n\n\n**Evaluating Keypad Logic**\n\nI\'m now closely examining the `KeypadScreen` composable, paying particular attention to its interactions with `AuthViewModel`. I am focused on the data flow and how the composable observes state changes from the ViewModel. This includes ensuring proper injection of dependencies like `PinStorage` and `SosController` and ensuring effective communication via `onUnlockSuccess`. I\'m verifying the composable\'s responsiveness to ViewModel updates and considering how to improve the composable\'s testability.\n\n\n**Observing UI State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the composable observes and reacts to `AuthViewModel` state changes. I\'m leveraging `collectAsState` for `enteredPin` and `errorMessage`. The `LaunchedEffect` is key to responding to unlock events. I\'m exploring the setup of a `Surface` with `Column` structure with padding and constraints. I\'m looking at how I can present a simple `Icon` in a `Box`.\n\n\n**Designing UI Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the UI design within the KeypadScreen composable, starting with the Petal Health logo and associated text elements. I\'m ensuring proper sizing and placement of the logo, and I\'m updating the text for the app name and the prompt to enter the PIN. The layout now includes a row of PIN dots to visually represent the entered PIN length and spacing. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy to make the UI intuitive. I\'m thinking about colors and fonts for a consistent look.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Feedback**\n\nI\'m now implementing the error feedback display within the keypad screen, using `AnimatedVisibility` for displaying error messages when they occur. I\'m leveraging `MaterialTheme`\'s color scheme for consistency in both the background and error text. I am using `Text` composable for the error message, ensuring the text color matches the MaterialTheme error color.\n\n\n"
