  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Unlock Event**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining a single-shot event for successful PIN validation within `AuthViewModel.kt`. I\'ve chosen `MutableSharedFlow` with `replay = 0` and `extraBufferCapacity = 1` for the `_unlockEvent`. It\'s exposed as a `SharedFlow` called `unlockEvent`.\n\n\n**Refining Unlock Emission**\n\nI\'ve considered how `_unlockEvent` is emitted based on `PinVerificationResult`.  `tryEmit(Unit)` seems ideal with `extraBufferCapacity = 1`. This lets the event emit synchronously for both normal and duress PIN successes, without any dispatcher switching! I\'ve also reviewed the associated test file to ensure proper handling in the testing environment. I am updating `AuthViewModel.kt`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_737904"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Use extraBufferCapacity and tryEmit for immediate non-suspending unlock event delivery in AuthViewModel\", \"EndLine\":76, \"Instruction\":\"Update _unlockEvent to use extraBufferCapacity=1 and tryEmit\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  // Single-shot event emitted when either PIN successfully validates\\n  private val _unlockEvent = MutableSharedFlow<Unit>(replay = 0, extraBufferCapacity = 1)\\n  val unlockEvent: SharedFlow<Unit> = _unlockEvent.asSharedFlow()\\n\\n  fun onKeyClicked(key: String) {\\n    _errorMessage.value = null\\n    when (key) {\\n      \\\"CLEAR\\\" -> _enteredPin.value = \\\"\\\"\\n      \\\"BACK\\\" -> {\\n        if (_enteredPin.value.isNotEmpty()) {\\n          _enteredPin.value = _enteredPin.value.dropLast(1)\\n        }\\n      }\\n      else -> {\\n        if (_enteredPin.value.length < 4 && key.all { it.isDigit() }) {\\n          val newPin = _enteredPin.value + key\\n          _enteredPin.value = newPin\\n          if (newPin.length == 4) {\\n            verifyPin(newPin)\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  fun verifyPin(pin: String) {\\n    val result = pinStorage.verify(pin)\\n    when (result) {\\n      is PinVerificationResult.NormalPinSuccess -> {\\n        // Normal PIN: stops any ongoing SOS session and proceeds to disguise\\n        if (sosController.isSosActive) {\\n          sosController.stopSos()\\n        }\\n        _unlockEvent.tryEmit(Unit)\\n      }\\n      is PinVerificationResult.DuressPinSuccess -> {\\n        // Duress PIN: silently activates the central idempotent SOS workflow\\n        // Invokes startSos with trigger source \\\"duress_pin\\\"\\n        sosController.startSos(triggerSource = \\\"duress_pin\\\")\\n        _unlockEvent.tryEmit(Unit)\\n      }\", \"StartLine\":32, \"TargetContent\":\"  // Single-shot event emitted when either PIN successfully validates\\n  private val _unlockEvent = MutableSharedFlow<Unit>(replay = 0)\\n  val unlockEvent: SharedFlow<Unit> = _unlockEvent.asSharedFlow()\\n\\n  fun onKeyClicked(key: String) {\\n    _errorMessage.value = null\\n    when (key) {\\n      \\\"CLEAR\\\" -> _enteredPin.value = \\\"\\\"\\n      \\\"BACK\\\" -> {\\n        if (_enteredPin.value.isNotEmpty()) {\\n          _enteredPin.value = _enteredPin.value.dropLast(1)\\n        }\\n      }\\n      else -> {\\n        if (_enteredPin.value.length < 4 && key.all { it.isDigit() }) {\\n          val newPin = _enteredPin.value + key\\n          _enteredPin.value = newPin\\n          if (newPin.length == 4) {\\n            verifyPin(newPin)\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  fun verifyPin(pin: String) {\\n    val result = pinStorage.verify(pin)\\n    when (result) {\\n      is PinVerificationResult.NormalPinSuccess -> {\\n        // Normal PIN: stops any ongoing SOS session and proceeds to disguise\\n        if (sosController.isSosActive) {\\n          sosController.stopSos()\\n        }\\n        viewModelScope.launch {\\n          _unlockEvent.emit(Unit)\\n        }\\n      }\\n      is PinVerificationResult.DuressPinSuccess -> {\\n        // Duress PIN: silently activates the central idempotent SOS workflow\\n        // Invokes startSos with trigger source \\\"duress_pin\\\"\\n        sosController.startSos(triggerSource = \\\"duress_pin\\\")\\n        viewModelScope.launch {\\n          _unlockEvent.emit(Unit)\\n        }\\n      }\", \"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/auth/AuthViewModel.kt\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating AuthViewModel event emission\", \"toolSummary\":\"Use tryEmit in AuthViewModel\"}"
