  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Unlock Failure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on why `unlockEmitted` is false in lines 244 and 272. I\'m tracing the `unlockEvent` collection within the launch block to understand the control flow. The aim is to pinpoint the cause for the assertion failure, and thus uncover the reason for the missing unlock event.\n\n\n**Analyzing Coroutine Dispatching**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the coroutine dispatcher behavior in testing. My focus is on how `StandardTestDispatcher` delays the execution of launched coroutines, specifically the collector for `unlockEvent`. This queuing leads to dropped events from the `SharedFlow` because the collector hasn\'t started when `tryEmit` is called. The `replay = 0` setting further exacerbates this. I\'m considering using an `UnconfinedTestDispatcher` or increasing `replay` to 1 to address this timing issue.\n\n\n**Refining Collector Activation**\n\nI\'m now exploring specific strategies to ensure timely collector activation. I\'m considering using `UnconfinedTestDispatcher` or calling `testScheduler.runCurrent()` to force the collector to start before key clicks. These approaches aim to prevent event dropping by ensuring the `unlockEvent` is actively subscribed to the `SharedFlow` before any emissions occur. I\'m also still thinking about `replay` size in the `SharedFlow`.\n\n\n"
