  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m now drilling down into the user\'s need for a Demo Mode. I\'ve broken it down: the public interface will be \"Petal\" with period tracking. Access is via PIN, with a normal PIN unlocking the basic app, and a duress PIN triggering the SOS system. I am moving towards a strategy.\n\n\n**Refining the Demo Mode**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Demo Mode\'s specifics. When the duress PIN is used in demo mode, I\'ll display a temporary \"Emergency assistance active\" screen. This screen will display status updates. I\'ve got three status rows fleshed out: location sharing (contact list, statuses like \"Sending SMS\", timestamps, and links), voice recording (states like \"Recording,\" \"Uploading,\" and error messages), and the overall SOS session status. These elements will clearly reflect the system\'s real-time activities.\n\n\n"
