  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding New Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating the `demoConfigManager` into the `CloakApplication`. The application already offers various components like database interaction, SMS dispatch, location provision, and SOS control, among others. Adding the `demoConfigManager` by a lazy instantiation feels quite seamless, I think.\n\n\n**Defining State Models**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining state models within `com.example.core.sos`. I\'ve structured `ContactSmsStatus` to track SMS delivery with a `DeliveryStatus` enum that clearly outlines each stage. The `AudioRecordingStatus` enum also maps the various states of audio recording, and I\'ve created a sealed class `ChunkUploadStatus` to express chunk upload states. This includes \"Idle,\" \"Uploading,\" and detailed progress tracking.\n\n\n**Refining Upload States**\n\nI\'ve refined the `ChunkUploadStatus` sealed class further. I\'ve added `Uploaded`, `Retrying`, and `Failed` data classes to represent upload states, including chunk index, timestamps, and retry attempts, along with failure reasons. I\'ve also incorporated these statuses into the `SosState.Active` data class, so now the application status reports the progress of chunk uploads more precisely.\n\n\n**Improving SMS Dispatch**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enhancing the `SmsDispatcher`. I\'m thinking of creating a `DetailedContactDispatchResult` data class to track the outcome of each SMS dispatch. This will give me a more detailed view of the SMS sending process. Instead of just tracking the overall `sentCount`, I want to know the individual status for each contact. This detailed result would report if the message was submitted and any errors that might have occurred.\n\n\n**Detailing Dispatch Outcomes**\n\nI\'m now detailing SMS dispatch outcomes. If I don\'t have SMS permission, I will mark each contact as `WAITING_FOR_PERMISSION`. If there\'s an SMS exception, I will log the contact as `FAILED`. Otherwise, I\'ll log them as `SMS_SUBMITTED`. This avoids misleading the user, since I only display an \"SMS submitted\" status until true delivery confirmation. Now, I\'m checking audio recording permissions and statuses, too.\n\n\n**Tracking Chunk Uploads**\n\nI\'ve got the `SosController` ready to receive status updates from the `SosForegroundService` using `updateAudioRecordingStatus` and `updateChunkUploadStatus` methods. I can now properly track chunk uploads. In `SosForegroundService`, I\'ll update the statuses after each stage of the upload process. On chunk readiness, I will send an `Uploading` status. On success, I\'ll send an `Uploaded` status with a timestamp. On failure, I\'ll send a `Failed` status with the error message, and on service stop I\'ll reset statuses.\n\n\n**Connecting the SOS Controller**\n\nI figured out how `SosController` and `SosForegroundService` interact! It\'s so clean: the service directly accesses the controller via the application context. Within `SosForegroundService.kt`, I\'m using `(application as? CloakApplication)?.sosController` to call the controller. It keeps the architecture intact and maintains the necessary decoupling.\n\n\n\n**Refining Unlock Events**\n\nI\'m now refining the unlock event logic. I\'m considering using an `AuthUnlockResult` sealed class, with `NormalUnlocked` and `DuressUnlocked` data objects, for better clarity. Alternatively, I\'m thinking of using a `MutableSharedFlow<Boolean>`, where `true` indicates a duress unlock. I\'ve got to check `KeypadScreen.kt` to make sure this all works.\n\n\n**Analyzing Navigation Logic**\n\nI\'m now carefully analyzing the navigation logic within `AppNavHost.kt`, particularly the handling of `onUnlockSuccess` within the `KeypadScreen` composable. I see that based on `isDuress` and whether `demoConfigManager.isDemoModeEnabled` is true, the navigation targets either the `DemoSos` or the `Tracker` screen. This is working perfectly!\n\n\n**Defining Demo SOS Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating a `DemoSosScreen` into the navigation flow. This screen will display status updates that match the honest statuses. It will show contacts, their delivery statuses, and location information. I\'m making sure to manage transitions, like the one to `FakeSleepFullScreen`, and preventing back navigation from the `DemoSosScreen` with a `BackHandler`. I\'ve added a navigation route, and made sure that it all ties into the main application navigation.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Recording**\n\nI\'m now implementing the voice recording interface to display its status accurately. I\'ll show states like \"Starting recording,\" \"Recording,\" \"Permission required,\" or \"Recording unavailable\" based on the actual service state. Also, I plan to display the upload status for recent chunks: \"Uploading,\" \"Uploaded,\" \"Retrying,\" or \"Failed\". I\'ll update these statuses in response to real events, using a clean design to keep the interface professional. Finally, I\'m integrating automatic transition to Fake-Sleep after a configurable delay, ensuring SOS is not interrupted.\n\n\n**Verifying Permission Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on permission handling within `DemoSosScreen`. If audio recording, SMS, or location permissions are missing, I\'m displaying the appropriate \"Waiting for permission\" message along with a button to request them. Upon permission grant, the related functionality immediately starts, i.e., recording audio or re-dispatching SMS, as intended. I\'m making sure that the demo screen accurately reflects these permission-related statuses.\n\n\n**Displaying Location Data**\n\nI\'m now displaying location data within the demo screen. With all permissions granted, I present the live GPS coordinates, formatted with a timestamp, and a direct Google Maps link. The contact statuses show each contact. The audio recording status, session details, and countdown banner all present, just like in real-time.\n\n\n"
