  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Demo Mode Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the \"Hackathon Demo Mode\" configuration card for the Settings. I\'ve fleshed out its basic structure: a title (\"Hackathon Demo Mode\") and a description (\"For presentation and judging. When enabled, entering the Duress PIN displays a temporary visible status screen (emergency contacts, GPS location\"). This card will be essential for presentations and judging situations.\n\n\n**Defining Demo Mode Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component design for \"Hackathon Demo Mode.\" I\'ve specified `DemoConfigManager.kt` to handle preferences, including `isDemoModeEnabled` (defaulting to disabled) and `transitionDelaySeconds`. I\'m also planning enhancements to `SosState.kt`, `SosController.kt`, and `SmsDispatcher.kt` to include various statuses related to demo mode: contact SMS, location timestamp, audio recording, and permissions.\n\n\n**Detailing Statuses and Permissions**\n\nI\'m working on the data structures. I have finalized `hasAudioPermission: Boolean`, which will be a part of the `Permission: Boolean` object. Additionally, I am finalizing the `ContactSmsStatus` object that contains `name: String`, `phoneNumber: String`, and `status: String`. Also, I am finalizing the `AudioRecordingStatus` object with statuses such as \"Idle\", \"Starting recording\", and so on. Lastly, I\'m defining the `ChunkUploadStatus` statuses, including \"Idle,\" \"Uploading,\" and \"Uploaded.\"\n\n\n**Refining Service Statuses**\n\nI\'m now detailing the `SosForegroundService.kt` statuses. When starting audio capture, I report \"Recording\" if mic permission is granted. Within the `AudioChunkRecorder` callback, I update to \"Uploading chunk #${chunkIndex + 1}.\" After a successful `supabaseRepo.uploadAudioChunk`, I\'ll update the `chunkUploadStatus` to \"Uploaded.\" I am also finalizing how contact statuses, audio recording, and chunk uploads will be reported in relation to the main foreground service.\n\n\n**Finalizing Failure States**\n\nI\'m now detailing error handling for audio chunk uploads, reporting \"Failed chunk #${chunkIndex + 1}: ${e.message}\" upon failure. If mic permission is denied, I will report \"Permission required.\" I\'m also focusing on the Compose screen for Demo Mode. I have a dedicated `DemoSosScreen.kt` component with a red/amber warning badge and headline. The screen includes location sharing details with contact statuses, a progress bar, and location information.\n\n\n**Defining Screen Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the DemoSosScreen UI, specifically focusing on the new `LocationPermissionRequired` state. I\'ve integrated a button to request permissions. I\'m also planning the \"Voice Recording\" section, with a status badge for different states, and upload status. Finally, I\'m integrating the SOS session telemetry and `FakeSleepFullScreen.kt` components. The \"Transition to Fake-Sleep\" button will now have an immediate transition.\n\n\n**Implementing Duress Navigation**\n\nI\'ve added the new routes `DemoSos` and `FakeSleep` to `Screen.kt`. I\'ve updated `KeypadScreen` and `AuthViewModel` to emit `isDuress = true` when the Duress PIN is entered. Now, in `AppNavHost`, if `isDuress` is true and demo mode is enabled, it navigates to `DemoSosScreen`; otherwise, it goes to `Tracker`. The `DemoSosScreen` then transitions to `FakeSleep` upon navigation.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1000705"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.core.demo\\n\\nimport android.content.Context\\nimport android.content.SharedPreferences\\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.MutableStateFlow\\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.StateFlow\\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.asStateFlow\\n\\n/**\\n * Manages developer/demo configuration for hackathon presentations.\\n * When enabled, duress PIN entry displays an honest visible SOS demonstration screen\\n * before automatically transitioning to the black Fake-Sleep screen.\\n *\\n * Disabled by default in production.\\n */\\nclass DemoConfigManager(context: Context) {\\n\\n  companion object {\\n    private const val PREFS_NAME = \\\"cloak_demo_prefs\\\"\\n    private const val KEY_DEMO_ENABLED = \\\"demo_mode_enabled\\\"\\n    private const val KEY_TRANSITION_DELAY_SECONDS = \\\"demo_transition_delay_seconds\\\"\\n    const val DEFAULT_DELAY_SECONDS = 8\\n    const val MIN_DELAY_SECONDS = 3\\n    const val MAX_DELAY_SECONDS = 30\\n  }\\n\\n  private val prefs: SharedPreferences =\\n    context.getSharedPreferences(PREFS_NAME, Context.MODE_PRIVATE)\\n\\n  private val _isDemoModeEnabled = MutableStateFlow(\\n    prefs.getBoolean(KEY_DEMO_ENABLED, false)\\n  )\\n  val isDemoModeEnabledFlow: StateFlow<Boolean> = _isDemoModeEnabled.asStateFlow()\\n\\n  val isDemoModeEnabled: Boolean\\n    get() = _isDemoModeEnabled.value\\n\\n  private val _transitionDelaySeconds = MutableStateFlow(\\n    prefs.getInt(KEY_TRANSITION_DELAY_SECONDS, DEFAULT_DELAY_SECONDS)\\n  )\\n  val transitionDelaySecondsFlow: StateFlow<Int> = _transitionDelaySeconds.asStateFlow()\\n\\n  val transitionDelaySeconds: Int\\n    get() = _transitionDelaySeconds.value\\n\\n  fun setDemoModeEnabled(enabled: Boolean) {\\n    _isDemoModeEnabled.value = enabled\\n    prefs.edit().putBoolean(KEY_DEMO_ENABLED, enabled).apply()\\n  }\\n\\n  fun setTransitionDelaySeconds(seconds: Int) {\\n    val clamped = seconds.coerceIn(MIN_DELAY_SECONDS, MAX_DELAY_SECONDS)\\n    _transitionDelaySeconds.value = clamped\\n    prefs.edit().putInt(KEY_TRANSITION_DELAY_SECONDS, clamped).apply()\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create DemoConfigManager to manage demo mode toggle and delay settings\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/core/demo/DemoConfigManager.kt\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating DemoConfigManager\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create DemoConfigManager\"}"
